{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'schema_version|\\\"learner\\\"|\\\"overview\\\"|\\\"formation\\\"' content/entries/5C0F.json content/dossiers/5C0F.json; cat content/entries/5C0F.json; cat content/dossiers/5C0F.json\"","aggregated_output":"/home/catalin/.profile: line 29: /tmp/mfc-uv-bin/env: No such file or directory\ncontent/entries/5C0F.json:16:  \"formation\": {\ncontent/entries/5C0F.json:88:  \"schema_version\": 2,\ncontent/entries/5C0F.json:275:  \"learner\": {\ncontent/entries/5C0F.json:276:    \"overview\": {\n{\n  \"character\": \"小\",\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"text\": \"小 means “small.” Its present form has a long central stroke between two shorter side strokes. Early marks are interpreted either as abstract signs of smallness or as fine sand grains; their referent remains disputed.\",\n    \"evidence_ids\": [\n      \"X-21e5c27b88aea75dc33a\",\n      \"X-9337d44faa93154e5b08\",\n      \"X-2a90e282a2ff3f19511d\",\n      \"X-eca33181dc16b0f2f777\",\n      \"X-5385acd88b51f476d32e\",\n      \"X-b8ded469510aa9455741\",\n      \"E6\",\n      \"E7\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"formation\": {\n    \"text\": \"小 has no settled account of what its early marks represent: analyses describe abstract signs of smallness, raindrops or scattered objects, or fine sand grains. The sand-grain account treats 小 as an early graph of 沙, but neither the depicted referent nor a sound-based borrowing is established. Accounts also describe 小 and 少 as sharing an early graph before they were differentiated; one account says 少’s lower dot became a diagonal stroke. In small-seal script, the central dot became a vertical stroke between two side marks. Shuowen’s analysis of this later form as 八 plus 丨 is a historical interpretation, not evidence of the original construction.\",\n    \"evidence_ids\": [\n      \"E3\",\n      \"X-21e5c27b88aea75dc33a\",\n      \"X-9337d44faa93154e5b08\",\n      \"X-7098042d6576a6e2edc8\",\n      \"X-6a67a2eba00317f0db96\",\n      \"X-2a90e282a2ff3f19511d\",\n      \"X-1ba7a1471a7e7d07ce0d\",\n      \"X-220d6fa8a217b3555938\",\n      \"X-a036255ebabd78a9e34e\",\n      \"X-803fd94611bb57f92df9\",\n      \"X-5385acd88b51f476d32e\",\n      \"X-5ac63eb9bb056d4dc7cb\",\n      \"X-b8ded469510aa9455741\",\n      \"X-c673b3b25eff702eb8d9\"\n    ],\n    \"type\": \"pictographic\"\n  },\n  \"components\": [],\n  \"history\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Oracle-bone and bronze forms are described as three dots. In small-seal script, the central dot lengthened into a vertical stroke. The curated image is a modern redraw of that script style, not an ancient artifact; the graphic change does not identify what the earlier marks represented.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\n        \"X-21e5c27b88aea75dc33a\",\n        \"X-2a90e282a2ff3f19511d\",\n        \"X-a036255ebabd78a9e34e\",\n        \"X-eca33181dc16b0f2f777\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Shuowen parses the seal form as 八 and 丨, explaining the marks as dividing something. Later analyses treat this as a reinterpretation of an altered form. Accounts also describe 小 and 少 as once sharing a graph before later differentiation, though their detailed graphic and lexical relationship remains unsettled.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\n        \"E3\",\n        \"E4\",\n        \"X-7098042d6576a6e2edc8\",\n        \"X-6a67a2eba00317f0db96\",\n        \"X-2a90e282a2ff3f19511d\",\n        \"X-266b8f35d92e78d22ad7\",\n        \"X-b8ded469510aa9455741\",\n        \"X-c673b3b25eff702eb8d9\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"uncertainties\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The earliest marks may indicate smallness abstractly or depict fine sand grains. The sand analysis does not establish the grains’ name or pronunciation, or show that 沙 was written by reusing 小 for a similar-sounding word.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\n        \"X-9337d44faa93154e5b08\",\n        \"X-2a90e282a2ff3f19511d\",\n        \"X-1ba7a1471a7e7d07ce0d\",\n        \"X-220d6fa8a217b3555938\",\n        \"X-a036255ebabd78a9e34e\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The cited oracle-bone use 小雨 is reported as an early example, but its artifact has no absolute date here. Other old uses include time expressions and status-related terms; their dates and connection with “small” are unresolved.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\n        \"X-7c4ee97c98a3f9f753ae\",\n        \"X-2a90e282a2ff3f19511d\",\n        \"X-220d6fa8a217b3555938\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"小 is reported as a sound element in 雀, but the historical sound relation remains disputed. In the supplied Baxter–Sagart reconstructions, 小 *[s]ewʔ and 雀 *[ts]ewk do not show an obvious rhyme match.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\n        \"X-b1e6b91540b7c6134706\",\n        \"X-af8f4361c990e6a92f5e\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": 2,\n  \"meaning_history\": {\n    \"senses\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"小:small\",\n        \"gloss\": \"small\",\n        \"period\": \"Oracle-bone use; absolute date unresolved\",\n        \"certainty\": \"established\",\n        \"status\": \"historical\",\n        \"text\": \"An oracle-bone example 小雨 is reported with 小 meaning “small.” This is a documented early use, not proof of the character’s hypothetical original referent.\",\n        \"evidence_ids\": [\n          \"X-7c4ee97c98a3f9f753ae\",\n          \"X-2a90e282a2ff3f19511d\",\n          \"X-220d6fa8a217b3555938\",\n          \"X-b8ded469510aa9455741\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"小:afternoon-time-expression\",\n        \"gloss\": \"afternoon time expression\",\n        \"period\": \"Dating unresolved\",\n        \"certainty\": \"established\",\n        \"status\": \"historical\",\n        \"text\": \"小食 is reported as an expression for an afternoon time. Its relation to the sense “small” is unresolved.\",\n        \"evidence_ids\": [\n          \"X-7c4ee97c98a3f9f753ae\",\n          \"X-220d6fa8a217b3555938\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"小:dusk-time-expression\",\n        \"gloss\": \"dusk time expression\",\n        \"period\": \"Dating unresolved\",\n        \"certainty\": \"established\",\n        \"status\": \"historical\",\n        \"text\": \"小采 is reported as an expression for dusk. Its chronology and relation to the sense “small” are unresolved.\",\n        \"evidence_ids\": [\n          \"X-7c4ee97c98a3f9f753ae\",\n          \"X-220d6fa8a217b3555938\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"小:small-current\",\n        \"gloss\": \"small; tiny; insignificant\",\n        \"period\": \"Current\",\n        \"certainty\": \"established\",\n        \"status\": \"current\",\n        \"text\": \"小 is used with the sense “small,” including “tiny” and “insignificant.”\",\n        \"evidence_ids\": [\n          \"E6\",\n          \"E7\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"developments\": [],\n    \"limitations\": [\n      {\n        \"text\": \"The available examples do not establish a dated semantic path between early and current uses, or between “small” and the reported time expressions or status-related uses.\",\n        \"evidence_ids\": [\n          \"X-7c4ee97c98a3f9f753ae\",\n          \"X-266b8f35d92e78d22ad7\",\n          \"X-220d6fa8a217b3555938\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"relationships\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"小->雀:phonetic_element_in\",\n      \"subject\": {\n        \"kind\": \"character\",\n        \"id\": \"小\"\n      },\n      \"object\": {\n        \"kind\": \"character\",\n        \"id\": \"雀\"\n      },\n      \"predicate\": \"phonetic_element_in\",\n      \"context_character\": \"小\",\n      \"certainty\": \"disputed\",\n      \"text\": \"小 is reported as a sound element in 雀, which is also described as contributing the sense “small bird.” This proposed sound role is not explained by the supplied Baxter–Sagart forms: 小 *[s]ewʔ and 雀 *[ts]ewk show no obvious rhyme match, and no sound-change account is established.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\n        \"X-b1e6b91540b7c6134706\",\n        \"X-af8f4361c990e6a92f5e\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"小~少:variant_of\",\n      \"subject\": {\n        \"kind\": \"character\",\n        \"id\": \"小\"\n      },\n      \"object\": {\n        \"kind\": \"character\",\n        \"id\": \"少\"\n      },\n      \"predicate\": \"variant_of\",\n      \"context_character\": \"小\",\n      \"certainty\": \"probable\",\n      \"text\": \"Accounts describe 小 and 少 as sharing an early graph before later differentiation; one account says 少’s lower mark became a diagonal stroke. This supports a qualified graphic relationship, not a direction in which one character derives from the other.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\n        \"X-9337d44faa93154e5b08\",\n        \"X-7098042d6576a6e2edc8\",\n        \"X-6a67a2eba00317f0db96\",\n        \"X-b8ded469510aa9455741\",\n        \"X-c673b3b25eff702eb8d9\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"meaning:小:small\",\n      \"subject\": {\n        \"kind\": \"character\",\n        \"id\": \"小\"\n      },\n      \"object\": {\n        \"kind\": \"sense\",\n        \"id\": \"小:small\"\n      },\n      \"predicate\": \"has_sense\",\n      \"context_character\": \"小\",\n      \"certainty\": \"established\",\n      \"text\": \"An oracle-bone example 小雨 is reported with 小 meaning “small.” This is a documented early use, not proof of the character’s hypothetical original referent.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\n        \"X-7c4ee97c98a3f9f753ae\",\n        \"X-2a90e282a2ff3f19511d\",\n        \"X-220d6fa8a217b3555938\",\n        \"X-b8ded469510aa9455741\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"meaning:小:afternoon-time-expression\",\n      \"subject\": {\n        \"kind\": \"character\",\n        \"id\": \"小\"\n      },\n      \"object\": {\n        \"kind\": \"sense\",\n        \"id\": \"小:afternoon-time-expression\"\n      },\n      \"predicate\": \"has_sense\",\n      \"context_character\": \"小\",\n      \"certainty\": \"established\",\n      \"text\": \"小食 is reported as an expression for an afternoon time. Its relation to the sense “small” is unresolved.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\n        \"X-7c4ee97c98a3f9f753ae\",\n        \"X-220d6fa8a217b3555938\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"meaning:小:dusk-time-expression\",\n      \"subject\": {\n        \"kind\": \"character\",\n        \"id\": \"小\"\n      },\n      \"object\": {\n        \"kind\": \"sense\",\n        \"id\": \"小:dusk-time-expression\"\n      },\n      \"predicate\": \"has_sense\",\n      \"context_character\": \"小\",\n      \"certainty\": \"established\",\n      \"text\": \"小采 is reported as an expression for dusk. Its chronology and relation to the sense “small” are unresolved.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\n        \"X-7c4ee97c98a3f9f753ae\",\n        \"X-220d6fa8a217b3555938\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"meaning:小:small-current\",\n      \"subject\": {\n        \"kind\": \"character\",\n        \"id\": \"小\"\n      },\n      \"object\": {\n        \"kind\": \"sense\",\n        \"id\": \"小:small-current\"\n      },\n      \"predicate\": \"has_sense\",\n      \"context_character\": \"小\",\n      \"certainty\": \"established\",\n      \"text\": \"小 is used with the sense “small,” including “tiny” and “insignificant.”\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\n        \"E6\",\n        \"E7\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"learner\": {\n    \"overview\": {\n      \"text\": \"小 means “small” and is written with a long central stroke between two shorter side strokes. The early marks are interpreted either as signs of smallness or as fine sand grains; their referent remains disputed.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\n        \"X-21e5c27b88aea75dc33a\",\n        \"X-9337d44faa93154e5b08\",\n        \"X-2a90e282a2ff3f19511d\",\n        \"X-eca33181dc16b0f2f777\",\n        \"X-5385acd88b51f476d32e\",\n        \"E6\",\n        \"E7\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"components\": [],\n    \"takeaway\": null\n  },\n  \"historical_glyphs\": {\n    \"items\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"小-seal\",\n        \"image_url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/%E5%B0%8F-seal.svg\",\n        \"source_url\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%B0%8F-seal.svg\",\n        \"source_title\": \"File:小-seal.svg\",\n        \"period\": \"Modern vector redraw of the Shuowen small-seal form; depicts an ancient script style, not a dated artifact\",\n        \"tradition\": \"Small seal script (小篆), Shuowen style\",\n        \"caption\": \"This modern redraw shows 小 in Shuowen small-seal style. The central dot has become a vertical stroke between two side marks; this later shape does not settle what the earlier marks represented.\",\n        \"alt\": \"Three black strokes: a long central vertical stroke between two shorter, slightly curved side strokes.\",\n        \"selection_reason\": \"It illustrates the seal-script form and the described graphic change while keeping the disputed interpretation of the earlier marks open.\",\n        \"rights\": \"Public-domain dedication for the modern vector representation; Commons page also records CC0 information.\",\n        \"rights_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\",\n        \"evidence_ids\": [\n          \"X-21e5c27b88aea75dc33a\",\n          \"X-eca33181dc16b0f2f777\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"limitations\": [\n      {\n        \"text\": \"This is a modern redraw, not an ancient inscription image. The earlier marks are interpreted either as abstract signs of smallness or as fine sand grains, and their referent remains uncertain.\",\n        \"evidence_ids\": [\n          \"X-9337d44faa93154e5b08\",\n          \"X-2a90e282a2ff3f19511d\",\n          \"X-eca33181dc16b0f2f777\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E1\",\n      \"source\": \"makemeahanzi\",\n      \"field\": \"hanzi.etymology_notes[0]\",\n      \"text\": \"Dividing 八 by a line 亅\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E2\",\n      \"source\": \"dong_chinese\",\n      \"field\": \"hanzi.etymology_notes[1]\",\n      \"text\": \"Pictograph of three small dots, representing grains of sand or rice, to convey the meaning \\\"small\\\".\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E3\",\n      \"source\": \"shuowen_jiezi\",\n      \"field\": \"hanzi.etymology_notes[2]\",\n      \"text\": \"物之微也。从八，丨見而分之。凡小之屬皆从小。\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E4\",\n      \"source\": \"wiktionary\",\n      \"field\": \"hanzi.etymology_notes[3]\",\n      \"text\": \"Two possible interpretations:\\n* Ideogram (指事) – three small dots > small.\\n* Pictogram (象形) – three granules of sand – original character of 沙 (OC *sraːl, *sraːls) > small.\\nStarting from some bronze inscriptions, the dots have become elongated. Based on this form, Shuowen erroneously considers it to be an ideogrammic compound (會意 /会意): 八 (“to divide; to separate”) + 丨 (“small object”).\\nCompare with 少 (OC *hmjewʔ, *hmjews), represented by four dots in its oracle bone script form. Unrelated to the bottom part of 京, 示, 尞, 尗, and 原.\\nOften thought to be related to 少 (OC *hmjewʔ, *hmjews) (e.g. Wang, 1982), but Schuessler (2007) points out that the alternation between Middle Chinese /s-/ and /ɕ-/ within a word family is exceptional.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E5\",\n      \"source\": \"shuowen_jiezi\",\n      \"field\": \"hanzi.shuowen.explanation\",\n      \"text\": \"物之微也。从八，丨見而分之。凡小之屬皆从小。\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E6\",\n      \"source\": \"merged_record\",\n      \"field\": \"hanzi.definitions\",\n      \"text\": \"small, tiny, insignificant\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_metadata\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E7\",\n      \"source\": \"merged_record\",\n      \"field\": \"hanzi.readings\",\n      \"text\": \"{\\\"cantonese\\\": \\\"siu2\\\", \\\"japanese_kun\\\": \\\"CHIISAI KO O\\\", \\\"japanese_on\\\": \\\"SHOU\\\", \\\"korean\\\": \\\"SO\\\", \\\"mandarin\\\": \\\"xiǎo\\\", \\\"tang\\\": \\\"*siɛ̌u\\\", \\\"vietnamese\\\": \\\"tiểu\\\"}\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_metadata\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E8\",\n      \"source\": \"merged_record\",\n      \"field\": \"hanzi.historical_phonology\",\n      \"text\": \"[{\\\"gloss\\\": \\\"small\\\", \\\"gsr\\\": \\\"1149a\\\", \\\"middle_chinese\\\": \\\"sjewX\\\", \\\"old_chinese\\\": \\\"*[s]ewʔ\\\"}, {\\\"old_chinese_zhengzhang\\\": \\\"*smewʔ\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"zhengzhang_wikt\\\"}, {\\\"old_chinese_zhengzhang\\\": \\\"*smewʔ\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"zhengzhang_wikt\\\"}, {\\\"fanqie\\\": \\\"私兆\\\", \\\"middle_chinese_guangyun\\\": \\\"心開三宵上\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"guangyun\\\"}, {\\\"old_chinese_zhengzhang\\\": \\\"smewʔ\\\", \\\"rhyme_group\\\": \\\"宵\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"zhengzhang\\\"}]\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_metadata\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E9\",\n      \"source\": \"kanjidic2_via_build_kanji\",\n      \"field\": \"kanji.definition\",\n      \"text\": \"Little; Small\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_metadata\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E10\",\n      \"source\": \"kanjidic2_via_build_kanji\",\n      \"field\": \"kanji.readings\",\n      \"text\": \"{\\\"japanese_kun\\\": \\\"ちい.さい こ- お- さ-\\\", \\\"japanese_on\\\": \\\"ショウ\\\"}\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_metadata\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E11\",\n      \"source\": \"ids_analysis\",\n      \"field\": \"kanji.etymology_notes[4]\",\n      \"text\": \"Etymological analysis: 會意\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-874259a2b827e31d1455\",\n      \"source\": \"Academia Sinica, Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"小 字形演變\",\n      \"text\": \"The database identifies oracle-bone and bronze forms, and gives two possible interpretations of their marks: three small dots symbolizing smallness, or grains of sand scattered around. It says that in small-seal script the central dot became a vertical stroke separating the two others.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n      \"title\": \"漢字「小」：字形演變\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-21e5c27b88aea75dc33a\",\n      \"source\": \"Academia Sinica, Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"甲骨文、金文、小篆字形\",\n      \"text\": \"The page labels the displayed stages oracle bone, bronze, small-seal, and Shuowen. Its account describes the seal form as a graphic alteration of earlier dots; the shapes alone do not establish the identity of a depicted object.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n      \"title\": \"漢字「小」：字形演變\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-9337d44faa93154e5b08\",\n      \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n      \"field\": \"甲骨文及構形初義\",\n      \"text\": \"The database records competing analyses: three small dots signifying smallness, attributed to Shang Chengzuo and Yu Xingwu; or 小 as an early graph of 沙, depicting fine sand grains, attributed to Ma Xulun. It also says 小 and 少 were originally one graph and later differentiated.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n      \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-7c4ee97c98a3f9f753ae\",\n      \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n      \"field\": \"甲骨文詞例及金文用例\",\n      \"text\": \"It reports oracle-bone 小 meaning ‘small,’ citing 《粹》1004 小雨; it separately reports 小食 as an afternoon time expression and 小采 as an evening expression. For bronze inscriptions it gives 嬴霝德鼎 小鼎 and notes 小子 for young aristocratic sons and lower officials, and 小臣 for officials subordinate to rulers. The page supplies no absolute dates for these cited artifacts or semantic developments.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"historical_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n      \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-7098042d6576a6e2edc8\",\n      \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n      \"field\": \"少 entry, graphic and usage account\",\n      \"text\": \"It says oracle-bone forms of 小/少 could have four dots and were used in the same way; later the three-dot graph was used for 小 and four-dot form for 少. In bronze forms, the lowest dot of 少 extended into a diagonal stroke. The page cites bronze uses of 少 for ‘few’ and ‘young,’ and a later case where 少 is read as 小. This supports graphic differentiation and shared early use, but does not settle the more specific proposed sand-grain referent.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"historical_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n      \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-6a67a2eba00317f0db96\",\n      \"source\": \"Academia Sinica, Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"少 字形演變\",\n      \"text\": \"The database states that 少 and 小 were originally one graph depicting fine sand grains, with ‘small’ as the original meaning; in bronze inscriptions the bottom dot of 少 became a diagonal stroke, distinguishing it from 小. This is a clear assertion of the shared-origin analysis, while CUHK presents that relationship alongside competing accounts of 小’s earliest formation.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"少\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10271\",\n      \"title\": \"漢字「少」：字形演變\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-2a90e282a2ff3f19511d\",\n      \"source\": \"《常用漢字二百字探源》 (PDF), entry 小\",\n      \"field\": \"字形探源 and 字義探源, pp. 20–21\",\n      \"text\": \"The book lists oracle-bone and bronze examples and says both scripts write 小 with three dots. It reports disagreement over what the dots depict, including raindrops, scattered objects, or fine smallness; it judges an abstract indicator-of-smallness analysis plausible. It says later dots lengthened into lines and rejects Shuowen’s parsing of the seal form as 八 plus 丨 as an error based on the later shape. It cites oracle-bone examples 小雨, 小風, and 小牢 for the ‘small’ use. This provides another account of the dots and the alleged graphic reinterpretation, not independent proof that they depict sand.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"scholarly_reference\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.yjcn.nl/wp/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/%E5%B8%B8%E7%94%A8%E6%BC%A2%E5%AD%97%E4%BA%8C%E7%99%BE%E5%AD%97%E6%8E%A2%E6%BA%90%EF%BC%88%E9%87%91%E7%9C%9F%E5%A7%AC%EF%BC%89.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"常用漢字二百字探源\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-266b8f35d92e78d22ad7\",\n      \"source\": \"Ministry of Education, Taiwan, Dictionary of Chinese Character Variants\",\n      \"field\": \"說文釋形; 字樣說明; 釋義\",\n      \"text\": \"The dictionary reproduces Xu Shen’s analysis: 小 means ‘the subtle/small among things’ and is analyzed as 八 and 丨, ‘seen and divided.’ It preserves this as a historical dictionary account. Its modern senses include small in size or quantity, make smaller, briefly, young, low-ranking, and humble self-reference, with classical citations; the page does not establish a chronological order among those senses.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?educode=A01068&powerMode=2\",\n      \"title\": \"教育部《異體字字典》：小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-1ba7a1471a7e7d07ce0d\",\n      \"source\": \"Wiktionary, 小 entry (consulted for competing analysis and reconstruction display)\",\n      \"field\": \"Chinese Glyph origin; Middle Chinese and Old Chinese readings\",\n      \"text\": \"The entry presents both an indicator interpretation (three dots to mean small) and a pictorial sand-grain interpretation, the latter identifying 小 as an early graph of 沙. It labels the 八 plus 丨 analysis in Shuowen an erroneous interpretation of an altered seal form. Its displayed comparisons are Middle Chinese 小 sjewX, Baxter–Sagart Old Chinese *[s]ewʔ, and Zhengzhang *smewʔ. These are source-reported reconstructions, not interchangeable notations.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"dictionary_and_reconstruction_compilation\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%E5%B0%8F\",\n      \"title\": \"小 - Wiktionary\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-e79ea1cfe5b5aa959a40\",\n      \"source\": \"Baxter and Sagart, Old Chinese reconstruction version 1.1, 13 September 2014\",\n      \"field\": \"Reconstruction notation documentation\",\n      \"text\": \"The authors distinguish Middle Chinese transcription from reconstruction, explain that square brackets mark uncertain identity and parentheses uncertain presence, and identify the table as version 1.1. The locally supplied Baxter–Sagart row for 小 is 小, Mandarin xiǎo, MC sjewX, OC *[s]ewʔ, gloss ‘small’; the opened source PDF was verified as the authors’ version 1.1 table, but browser extraction did not expose the specific 小 row. The value here is therefore reported as checked against the provided local row, not as an independently extracted online row.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"reconstruction_reference_and_local_row\",\n      \"url\": \"https://sites.lsa.umich.edu/ocbaxtersagart/wp-content/uploads/sites/1415/2025/03/BaxterSagartOCbyRadStr2014-09-20.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"BaxterSagartOCbyRadStr2014-09-20\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-b1e6b91540b7c6134706\",\n      \"source\": \"Chinese University of Hong Kong, Multi-function Chinese Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"雀 entry: component roles\",\n      \"text\": \"The database describes 小 in 雀 as both contributing the sense ‘small bird’ and functioning as a sound element. This is evidence for a phonetic role of 小 in that compound, but it does not establish that sand was the original object represented by 小. No comparison of 雀’s and 小’s readings in one reconstructed system was verified in this research.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"雀\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n      \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-a6339f9c0072cd12d52a\",\n      \"source\": \"Unicode Consortium, Unihan Database Lookup\",\n      \"field\": \"Unihan lookup instructions and database scope\",\n      \"text\": \"The official page says the lookup interface provides property data for individual ideographs, including readings, and that data are based on Unicode 18.0.0. The exact 小 record could not be accessed through the required per-character endpoint. The supplied local Unihan_Readings.txt row for 小 gives kMandarin xiǎo; it is cited here as a local row check, not as externally verified character-specific Unicode evidence.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"official_database_documentation_and_local_row\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.unicode.org/charts/unihan.html\",\n      \"title\": \"Unihan Database Lookup\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-220d6fa8a217b3555938\",\n      \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n      \"field\": \"構形初義; 甲骨文用例; 金文用例\",\n      \"text\": \"The database records two competing origin analyses: three dots representing smallness, attributed to Shang Chengzuo and Yu Xingwu; or 小 as an early graph of 沙 depicting fine sand, attributed to Ma Xulun. It says 小 and 少 were one graph before differentiation. It cites oracle-bone 小雨 (《粹》1004), 小食 for afternoon, 小采 for dusk, bronze 小鼎, and 小子/小臣 for young nobles or lower officials. It gives no absolute dates for the cited artifacts or semantic developments.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_and_historical_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n      \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-a036255ebabd78a9e34e\",\n      \"source\": \"Academia Sinica, Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"字形演變\",\n      \"text\": \"The page labels oracle-bone, bronze, small-seal and Shuowen stages. It asserts that the earlier marks depict scattered fine sand grains and says the middle dot in small-seal changed into a vertical stroke separating the other two. This is one source's analysis; the marks do not independently identify sand.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n      \"title\": \"漢字「小」：字形演變\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-eca33181dc16b0f2f777\",\n      \"source\": \"Wikimedia Commons\",\n      \"field\": \"Summary; original file; Licensing\",\n      \"text\": \"The inspected File page identifies 小-seal.svg as a modern vector depiction of 小 in Shuowen seal-script style and links its original image. The page states public-domain dedication for the representation, alongside CC0 information. This is a modern redraw, not an ancient artifact photograph.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"image_provenance_and_rights\",\n      \"url\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%B0%8F-seal.svg\",\n      \"title\": \"File:小-seal.svg\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-f6f7d68f09a02c854d24\",\n      \"source\": \"Academia Sinica, Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"智財權聲明\",\n      \"text\": \"The inspected rights notice reserves intellectual property in the site's content and limits use absent a separate agreement; it does not provide CC0 reuse terms. Accordingly, its page is used as linked evidence, not as an image asset.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"rights_notice\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/copyright.jsp\",\n      \"title\": \"智財權聲明\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-2829f816c26a5d71ec70\",\n      \"source\": \"Unicode Consortium, Unihan Database Lookup\",\n      \"field\": \"Per-character Unihan record\",\n      \"text\": \"The required individual record endpoint for 小 could not be opened in this run (internal fetch error). The supplied local Unihan row records kMandarin xiǎo, but is local data and is not independently verified here as a character-specific external record.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"access_failure_and_local_row_note\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5C0F\",\n      \"title\": \"Unihan Database Lookup\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-253281f9589a65c2d2a6\",\n      \"source\": \"Repository supplied local_primary_readings\",\n      \"field\": \"sources/unihan/Unihan_Readings.txt; kMandarin rows\",\n      \"text\": \"Supplied exact local rows: 小 xiǎo; 少 shǎo; 雀 què. These are current Mandarin metadata only, not evidence of ancient phonetic relationships. Their official individual Unihan click-through records for 小, 少, and 雀 were not verified as accessible in this run.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小; 少; 雀\",\n      \"kind\": \"local_reading_rows\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5C0F\",\n      \"title\": \"Unihan individual character lookup (endpoint unavailable)\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-af8f4361c990e6a92f5e\",\n      \"source\": \"Repository supplied local_primary_readings\",\n      \"field\": \"sources/baxter-sagart/baxtersagart.tsv; Baxter–Sagart 2014 rows\",\n      \"text\": \"Exact supplied rows: 小 xiǎo, MC sjewX, OC *[s]ewʔ (‘small’); 少 shǎo MC syewX OC *[s.t]ewʔ (‘few’) and shào MC syewH OC *[s-t]ewʔ-s (‘young’); 雀 què MC tsjak OC *[ts]ewk (‘sparrow’). These are Baxter–Sagart 2014 table notations, checked as local rows. The *[s]ewʔ and *[ts]ewk forms do not support an obvious rhyme match for a proposed 小→雀 sound role in that system; CUHK's component-role assertion can be reported as source-attributed, without treating the local forms as proof of a sound change.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小; 少; 雀\",\n      \"kind\": \"local_reconstruction_rows\",\n      \"url\": \"https://sites.lsa.umich.edu/ocbaxtersagart/wp-content/uploads/sites/1415/2025/03/BaxterSagartOCbyRadStr2014-09-20.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"BaxterSagartOCbyRadStr2014-09-20 (version 1.1)\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-dd1f049d3ded734931ba\",\n      \"source\": \"李學勤主編,《字源》, 天津古籍出版社／遼寧人民出版社, 2012\",\n      \"field\": \"小 headword; PDF p. 76, printed p. 64; scanned headword and continuation checked on PDF p. 77, printed p. 65\",\n      \"text\": \"The scanned entry identifies 小 as pictographic and interprets its marks as tiny grains of dust or sand, calling it an early graph of 沙; it says the graph was extended to mean ‘small,’ opposite 大, and gives that sense in oracle-bone and bronze inscriptions. It cites 《粹》1004 for 小雨, then describes extensions to low status, contempt, and youth. It says the current form was corrupted in bronze inscriptions and treats Shuowen’s 八-plus-丨 account as an explanation of that altered form. The adjacent 少 entry says 小 and 少 were originally one graph, with similar use in oracle-bone texts, and later differentiated; its explanation continues onto printed p. 65. Direct scan inspection confirms the cited headword and passage. Forms checked against pixels: 小, 少, 沙, 八, 丨, 大, and the text’s citation 《粹》1004. The scan supports what this author asserts; it does not settle the disputed sand-grain interpretation.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"directly_inspected_book_scan\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.worldcat.org/search?q=9787552800692\",\n      \"title\": \"《字源》 (2012), PDF pp. 76–77; printed pp. 64–65\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-803fd94611bb57f92df9\",\n      \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n      \"field\": \"小: formation, early use and adjacent 少 entry\",\n      \"text\": \"The database reports two analyses of 小’s early marks: abstract dots for smallness, attributed to 商承祚 and 于省吾, or an early graph of 沙 depicting fine grains, attributed to 馬敘倫. It also describes 小 and 少 as an originally shared graph. Its examples include oracle-bone 小雨, time expressions 小食 and 小采, and bronze 小鼎, 小子 and 小臣. The page provides no absolute dates for these cited artifacts or usages, so it cannot alone establish a chronology among the senses.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_and_historical_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n      \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-5385acd88b51f476d32e\",\n      \"source\": \"金真姬,《常用漢字二百字探源》\",\n      \"field\": \"小, 字形探源／字義探源, PDF pp. 20–21; printed pp. 26–27\",\n      \"text\": \"The inspected entry reports disagreement about what the three dots represent, including raindrops, scattered objects or fine smallness. It favors an abstract indication of smallness and says later lengthened dots prompted Shuowen’s 八-plus-丨 analysis, which it rejects as based on the altered form. It cites oracle-bone 小雨, 小風 and 小牢 as uses for ‘small.’ This supports a competing scholarly account, not a settled referent for the dots.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"scholarly_reference\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.yjcn.nl/wp/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/%E5%B8%B8%E7用漢字二百字探源%EF%BC%88金真姬%EF%BC%89.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"《常用漢字二百字探源》, PDF pp. 20–21\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-5ac63eb9bb056d4dc7cb\",\n      \"source\": \"中央研究院, Academia Sinica Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"少 字形演變\",\n      \"text\": \"The page states that 少 and 小 were originally one graph depicting fine sand grains, with ‘small’ as the original meaning; it says the lower dot of 少 became a diagonal stroke in bronze inscriptions, distinguishing it from 小. This is an explicit shared-origin analysis, while other consulted sources retain competing analyses of 小’s dots.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"少\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10271\",\n      \"title\": \"漢字「少」：字形演變\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-b8ded469510aa9455741\",\n      \"source\": \"李學勤主編,《字源》\",\n      \"field\": \"小 headword; PDF p. 76, printed p. 64; continuation PDF p. 77, printed p. 65\",\n      \"text\": \"The inspected entry calls 小 pictographic, interpreting its marks as tiny dust or sand particles and describing 小 as an early graph of 沙. It says the graph extended to mean ‘small,’ opposite 大, and reports that sense in oracle-bone and bronze inscriptions, citing 《粹》1004 for 小雨. It describes later extensions to low status, contempt and youth. It says the graph had become corrupted in bronze inscriptions and treats Shuowen’s 八-plus-丨 account as an explanation of that altered form. The adjacent 少 entry says 小 and 少 were originally one graph, used similarly in oracle-bone texts, and later differentiated; its account continues on printed p. 65. Both attached page images were inspected. Forms checked against scan pixels: 小, 少, 沙, 八, 丨, 大, and 《粹》1004. This verifies what this author claims, not the disputed sand-grain interpretation.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"directly_inspected_book_scan\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.worldcat.org/search?q=9787552800692\",\n      \"title\": \"《字源》, 李學勤主編, 天津古籍出版社／遼寧人民出版社, 2012, PDF pp. 76–77; printed pp. 64–65\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-cfcd778e20a67d7860ec\",\n      \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n      \"field\": \"小 formation, early uses and adjacent 少, 沙 and 雀 records\",\n      \"text\": \"The database reports competing interpretations of 小’s early marks: abstract dots for smallness, attributed to 商承祚 and 于省吾, or an early graph of 沙 depicting fine grains, attributed to 馬敍倫. It says 小 and 少 were one graph before differentiation, and that oracle-bone forms could use four dots for 小/少. It reports 小雨, 小食 (afternoon), 小采 (dusk), and bronze 小鼎, 小子 and 小臣, without absolute dates for the cited artifacts or semantic developments. Its 沙 entry discusses several analyses of 沙 forms; thus the page does not establish that 沙 was borrowed phonetically from 小. Its 雀 entry says 小 contributes both ‘small bird’ and sound, while separately reporting varied early uses and graphic forms.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小; 少; 沙; 雀\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_and_historical_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n      \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-4029d7e014bdb7910f42\",\n      \"source\": \"中央研究院, Academia Sinica Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"小 字形演變\",\n      \"text\": \"The page labels oracle-bone, bronze, small-seal and Shuowen forms. It interprets the earlier marks as tiny sand grains scattered around, expressing smallness, and says the middle dot in small-seal script became a vertical stroke separating the two side marks. This is one source’s interpretation, not independent proof of the depicted referent.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n      \"title\": \"漢字「小」：字形演變\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-fe9ea9767e1da9fa626c\",\n      \"source\": \"教育部《異體字字典》, Taiwan Ministry of Education\",\n      \"field\": \"說文釋形; 釋義\",\n      \"text\": \"The dictionary preserves Xu Shen’s historical account: 小 means ‘the subtle/small among things’ and is analyzed as 八 and 丨, ‘seen and divided.’ It lists modern senses including small, make smaller, brief, young, lower-ranked, humble self-reference, slight degree and despise, with citations, but does not establish a chronological order among them.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?educode=A01068&powerMode=2\",\n      \"title\": \"教育部《異體字字典》：小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-9cae30a34adfac4e5d42\",\n      \"source\": \"Nohara, “The reconstruction of the word shao (少) in Old Chinese Phonology”\",\n      \"field\": \"少 and 小 sound relationship; discussion and reconstruction comparison, pp. 2–6, 16\",\n      \"text\": \"The inspected study summarizes two positions on the proposed sound relationship around 少: Zhengzhang and Pan allow relationships among 少, 小 and related forms through reconstructed nasal initials; Schuessler and Baxter–Sagart reject a 少–小 phonetic-series relationship, with Schuessler treating 小 as semantic rather than phonetic in the cited discussion. The study also documents that early spellings 少 and 小 can both represent the words ‘small’ and ‘few’ in some oracle-bone, bronze and Warring States materials, with orthographic practice differing across regions and periods. This supports caution about inferring a phonetic relation from shared early spelling or present form alone.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"少; 小\",\n      \"kind\": \"scholarly_study\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/339973841_The_reconstruction_of_the_word_shao_shao_in_Old_Chinese_Phonology_shaonoshangguyinnitsuite\",\n      \"title\": \"「少」の上古音について／The reconstruction of the word shao (少) in Old Chinese Phonology\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-142dfc94245bc8e052bc\",\n      \"source\": \"Baxter and Sagart, Old Chinese reconstruction version 1.1\",\n      \"field\": \"Search result for author-hosted reconstruction table; PDF could not be opened in this invocation\",\n      \"text\": \"Search surfaced the authors’ version 1.1 table PDF, but the browser failed to open it. No specific 小, 少, 沙 or 雀 row was independently inspected in this invocation, so no table readings are asserted here.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小; 少; 沙; 雀\",\n      \"kind\": \"access_failure\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ocbaxtersagart.lsait.lsa.umich.edu/BaxterSagartOCbyMandarinMC2014-09-20.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"Baxter-Sagart Old Chinese reconstruction, version 1.1\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-46ffd93eb016aa392f31\",\n      \"source\": \"李學勤主編,《字源》, 天津古籍出版社／遼寧人民出版社, 2012, ISBN 9787552800692\",\n      \"field\": \"小 headword; PDF p. 76, printed p. 64\",\n      \"text\": \"The entry calls 小 pictographic and interprets its marks as tiny dust or sand particles, an early graph of 沙. It says the graph was extended to mean ‘small,’ opposite 大, and cites oracle-bone and bronze uses, including 《粹》1004 小雨. It also describes extensions to low status, contempt and youth, and says the bronze form had become corrupted, prompting Shuowen’s 八-plus-丨 explanation. Both attached page images were inspected; the printed headword, cited forms 小, 沙, 大, 八, 丨 and 《粹》1004 are legible. This verifies the author’s account, not the disputed sand interpretation.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"directly_inspected_book_scan\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.worldcat.org/search?q=9787552800692\",\n      \"title\": \"《字源》, 李學勤主編, 2012, PDF p. 76; printed p. 64\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-c673b3b25eff702eb8d9\",\n      \"source\": \"李學勤主編,《字源》, 天津古籍出版社／遼寧人民出版社, 2012, ISBN 9787552800692\",\n      \"field\": \"Adjacent 少 entry; PDF p. 76 and continuation p. 77, printed pp. 64–65\",\n      \"text\": \"The adjacent 少 entry says 小 and 少 were originally one graph and were used alike in oracle-bone texts, then differentiated; it describes 少’s final diagonal stroke as a distinguishing mark. The entry continues onto printed p. 65. Both source scans were inspected; the relevant 少 and 小 forms are legible. This is the book author’s graphic account, not proof of a historical sound relationship.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"少; 小\",\n      \"kind\": \"directly_inspected_book_scan\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.worldcat.org/search?q=9787552800692\",\n      \"title\": \"《字源》, 李學勤主編, 2012, PDF pp. 76–77; printed pp. 64–65\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-047697228b315d31e79e\",\n      \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n      \"field\": \"小, 少 and 沙 records: formation, cited uses and graph components\",\n      \"text\": \"The 小 record presents two analyses of its early marks: abstract dots for smallness, attributed to 商承祚 and 于省吾, or an early graph of 沙 depicting fine sand grains, attributed to 馬敍倫. It reports 小雨, 小食 as an afternoon expression, 小采 as a dusk expression, and bronze uses including 小鼎, 小子 and 小臣, without absolute artifact dates. Its 少 record says early forms could overlap and that three-dot and four-dot spellings later distinguished 小 and 少. The 沙 account reports competing analyses of bronze uses, so the cited pages do not establish a phonetic borrowing of 沙 from 小.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小; 少; 沙\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_and_historical_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n      \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-0ec345d60e9fc6dc0872\",\n      \"source\": \"中央研究院, Academia Sinica Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"少 字形演變\",\n      \"text\": \"The database asserts that 少 and 小 were originally one graph depicting fine sand grains, with ‘small’ as the original meaning, and says the lowest dot of 少 became a diagonal stroke in bronze inscriptions. This supports that interpretation as a source-attributed account; CUHK presents competing analyses of 小’s marks.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"少\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10271\",\n      \"title\": \"漢字「少」：字形演變\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-1fc728b859bc4669b67d\",\n      \"source\": \"中央研究院, Academia Sinica Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"小 字形演變\",\n      \"text\": \"The page labels oracle-bone, bronze, small-seal and Shuowen forms. It interprets the earlier marks as scattered fine sand grains expressing smallness and says the middle dot became a vertical stroke separating the two side marks in small-seal script. This is the database’s interpretation, not independent proof of the marks’ referent.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n      \"title\": \"漢字「小」：字形演變\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-1b31b87c8aa5370dbe65\",\n      \"source\": \"Masaki Nohara, “The reconstruction of the word shao (少) in Old Chinese Phonology,” 中国語学 262 (2015), pp. 57–75\",\n      \"field\": \"少–小 phonetic relationship and early orthographic usage, especially PDF pp. 59–65\",\n      \"text\": \"Nohara reviews competing Old Chinese analyses. Zhengzhang and Pan allow links among 少, 小 and related forms via proposed nasal initials, while Schuessler and Baxter–Sagart reject a 少–小 phonetic-series relation in the discussion Nohara cites. Nohara argues that excavated-text spelling and sound evidence do not warrant treating the early graphic overlap as proof of a phonetic relationship. The paper also documents that 少 and 小 spellings could represent both ‘few’ and ‘small’ in some early materials, with regional and period differences.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"少; 小\",\n      \"kind\": \"scholarly_study\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/chuugokugogaku/2015/262/2015_57/_pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"「少」の上古音について／The reconstruction of the word shao (少) in Old Chinese Phonology\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"dossier\": {\n    \"character\": \"小\",\n    \"evidence\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"E1\",\n        \"source\": \"makemeahanzi\",\n        \"field\": \"hanzi.etymology_notes[0]\",\n        \"text\": \"Dividing 八 by a line 亅\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"E2\",\n        \"source\": \"dong_chinese\",\n        \"field\": \"hanzi.etymology_notes[1]\",\n        \"text\": \"Pictograph of three small dots, representing grains of sand or rice, to convey the meaning \\\"small\\\".\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"E3\",\n        \"source\": \"shuowen_jiezi\",\n        \"field\": \"hanzi.etymology_notes[2]\",\n        \"text\": \"物之微也。从八，丨見而分之。凡小之屬皆从小。\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"E4\",\n        \"source\": \"wiktionary\",\n        \"field\": \"hanzi.etymology_notes[3]\",\n        \"text\": \"Two possible interpretations:\\n* Ideogram (指事) – three small dots > small.\\n* Pictogram (象形) – three granules of sand – original character of 沙 (OC *sraːl, *sraːls) > small.\\nStarting from some bronze inscriptions, the dots have become elongated. Based on this form, Shuowen erroneously considers it to be an ideogrammic compound (會意 /会意): 八 (“to divide; to separate”) + 丨 (“small object”).\\nCompare with 少 (OC *hmjewʔ, *hmjews), represented by four dots in its oracle bone script form. Unrelated to the bottom part of 京, 示, 尞, 尗, and 原.\\nOften thought to be related to 少 (OC *hmjewʔ, *hmjews) (e.g. Wang, 1982), but Schuessler (2007) points out that the alternation between Middle Chinese /s-/ and /ɕ-/ within a word family is exceptional.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"E5\",\n        \"source\": \"shuowen_jiezi\",\n        \"field\": \"hanzi.shuowen.explanation\",\n        \"text\": \"物之微也。从八，丨見而分之。凡小之屬皆从小。\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"E6\",\n        \"source\": \"merged_record\",\n        \"field\": \"hanzi.definitions\",\n        \"text\": \"small, tiny, insignificant\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"imported_metadata\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"E7\",\n        \"source\": \"merged_record\",\n        \"field\": \"hanzi.readings\",\n        \"text\": \"{\\\"cantonese\\\": \\\"siu2\\\", \\\"japanese_kun\\\": \\\"CHIISAI KO O\\\", \\\"japanese_on\\\": \\\"SHOU\\\", \\\"korean\\\": \\\"SO\\\", \\\"mandarin\\\": \\\"xiǎo\\\", \\\"tang\\\": \\\"*siɛ̌u\\\", \\\"vietnamese\\\": \\\"tiểu\\\"}\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"imported_metadata\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"E8\",\n        \"source\": \"merged_record\",\n        \"field\": \"hanzi.historical_phonology\",\n        \"text\": \"[{\\\"gloss\\\": \\\"small\\\", \\\"gsr\\\": \\\"1149a\\\", \\\"middle_chinese\\\": \\\"sjewX\\\", \\\"old_chinese\\\": \\\"*[s]ewʔ\\\"}, {\\\"old_chinese_zhengzhang\\\": \\\"*smewʔ\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"zhengzhang_wikt\\\"}, {\\\"old_chinese_zhengzhang\\\": \\\"*smewʔ\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"zhengzhang_wikt\\\"}, {\\\"fanqie\\\": \\\"私兆\\\", \\\"middle_chinese_guangyun\\\": \\\"心開三宵上\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"guangyun\\\"}, {\\\"old_chinese_zhengzhang\\\": \\\"smewʔ\\\", \\\"rhyme_group\\\": \\\"宵\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"zhengzhang\\\"}]\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"imported_metadata\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"E9\",\n        \"source\": \"kanjidic2_via_build_kanji\",\n        \"field\": \"kanji.definition\",\n        \"text\": \"Little; Small\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"imported_metadata\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"E10\",\n        \"source\": \"kanjidic2_via_build_kanji\",\n        \"field\": \"kanji.readings\",\n        \"text\": \"{\\\"japanese_kun\\\": \\\"ちい.さい こ- お- さ-\\\", \\\"japanese_on\\\": \\\"ショウ\\\"}\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"imported_metadata\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"E11\",\n        \"source\": \"ids_analysis\",\n        \"field\": \"kanji.etymology_notes[4]\",\n        \"text\": \"Etymological analysis: 會意\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-874259a2b827e31d1455\",\n        \"source\": \"Academia Sinica, Character Database\",\n        \"field\": \"小 字形演變\",\n        \"text\": \"The database identifies oracle-bone and bronze forms, and gives two possible interpretations of their marks: three small dots symbolizing smallness, or grains of sand scattered around. It says that in small-seal script the central dot became a vertical stroke separating the two others.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n        \"title\": \"漢字「小」：字形演變\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-21e5c27b88aea75dc33a\",\n        \"source\": \"Academia Sinica, Character Database\",\n        \"field\": \"甲骨文、金文、小篆字形\",\n        \"text\": \"The page labels the displayed stages oracle bone, bronze, small-seal, and Shuowen. Its account describes the seal form as a graphic alteration of earlier dots; the shapes alone do not establish the identity of a depicted object.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n        \"title\": \"漢字「小」：字形演變\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-9337d44faa93154e5b08\",\n        \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n        \"field\": \"甲骨文及構形初義\",\n        \"text\": \"The database records competing analyses: three small dots signifying smallness, attributed to Shang Chengzuo and Yu Xingwu; or 小 as an early graph of 沙, depicting fine sand grains, attributed to Ma Xulun. It also says 小 and 少 were originally one graph and later differentiated.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n        \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-7c4ee97c98a3f9f753ae\",\n        \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n        \"field\": \"甲骨文詞例及金文用例\",\n        \"text\": \"It reports oracle-bone 小 meaning ‘small,’ citing 《粹》1004 小雨; it separately reports 小食 as an afternoon time expression and 小采 as an evening expression. For bronze inscriptions it gives 嬴霝德鼎 小鼎 and notes 小子 for young aristocratic sons and lower officials, and 小臣 for officials subordinate to rulers. The page supplies no absolute dates for these cited artifacts or semantic developments.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"historical_dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n        \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-7098042d6576a6e2edc8\",\n        \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n        \"field\": \"少 entry, graphic and usage account\",\n        \"text\": \"It says oracle-bone forms of 小/少 could have four dots and were used in the same way; later the three-dot graph was used for 小 and four-dot form for 少. In bronze forms, the lowest dot of 少 extended into a diagonal stroke. The page cites bronze uses of 少 for ‘few’ and ‘young,’ and a later case where 少 is read as 小. This supports graphic differentiation and shared early use, but does not settle the more specific proposed sand-grain referent.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"historical_dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n        \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-6a67a2eba00317f0db96\",\n        \"source\": \"Academia Sinica, Character Database\",\n        \"field\": \"少 字形演變\",\n        \"text\": \"The database states that 少 and 小 were originally one graph depicting fine sand grains, with ‘small’ as the original meaning; in bronze inscriptions the bottom dot of 少 became a diagonal stroke, distinguishing it from 小. This is a clear assertion of the shared-origin analysis, while CUHK presents that relationship alongside competing accounts of 小’s earliest formation.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"少\",\n        \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10271\",\n        \"title\": \"漢字「少」：字形演變\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-2a90e282a2ff3f19511d\",\n        \"source\": \"《常用漢字二百字探源》 (PDF), entry 小\",\n        \"field\": \"字形探源 and 字義探源, pp. 20–21\",\n        \"text\": \"The book lists oracle-bone and bronze examples and says both scripts write 小 with three dots. It reports disagreement over what the dots depict, including raindrops, scattered objects, or fine smallness; it judges an abstract indicator-of-smallness analysis plausible. It says later dots lengthened into lines and rejects Shuowen’s parsing of the seal form as 八 plus 丨 as an error based on the later shape. It cites oracle-bone examples 小雨, 小風, and 小牢 for the ‘small’ use. This provides another account of the dots and the alleged graphic reinterpretation, not independent proof that they depict sand.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"scholarly_reference\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.yjcn.nl/wp/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/%E5%B8%B8%E7%94%A8%E6%BC%A2%E5%AD%97%E4%BA%8C%E7%99%BE%E5%AD%97%E6%8E%A2%E6%BA%90%EF%BC%88%E9%87%91%E7%9C%9F%E5%A7%AC%EF%BC%89.pdf\",\n        \"title\": \"常用漢字二百字探源\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-266b8f35d92e78d22ad7\",\n        \"source\": \"Ministry of Education, Taiwan, Dictionary of Chinese Character Variants\",\n        \"field\": \"說文釋形; 字樣說明; 釋義\",\n        \"text\": \"The dictionary reproduces Xu Shen’s analysis: 小 means ‘the subtle/small among things’ and is analyzed as 八 and 丨, ‘seen and divided.’ It preserves this as a historical dictionary account. Its modern senses include small in size or quantity, make smaller, briefly, young, low-ranking, and humble self-reference, with classical citations; the page does not establish a chronological order among those senses.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?educode=A01068&powerMode=2\",\n        \"title\": \"教育部《異體字字典》：小\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-1ba7a1471a7e7d07ce0d\",\n        \"source\": \"Wiktionary, 小 entry (consulted for competing analysis and reconstruction display)\",\n        \"field\": \"Chinese Glyph origin; Middle Chinese and Old Chinese readings\",\n        \"text\": \"The entry presents both an indicator interpretation (three dots to mean small) and a pictorial sand-grain interpretation, the latter identifying 小 as an early graph of 沙. It labels the 八 plus 丨 analysis in Shuowen an erroneous interpretation of an altered seal form. Its displayed comparisons are Middle Chinese 小 sjewX, Baxter–Sagart Old Chinese *[s]ewʔ, and Zhengzhang *smewʔ. These are source-reported reconstructions, not interchangeable notations.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"dictionary_and_reconstruction_compilation\",\n        \"url\": \"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%E5%B0%8F\",\n        \"title\": \"小 - Wiktionary\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-e79ea1cfe5b5aa959a40\",\n        \"source\": \"Baxter and Sagart, Old Chinese reconstruction version 1.1, 13 September 2014\",\n        \"field\": \"Reconstruction notation documentation\",\n        \"text\": \"The authors distinguish Middle Chinese transcription from reconstruction, explain that square brackets mark uncertain identity and parentheses uncertain presence, and identify the table as version 1.1. The locally supplied Baxter–Sagart row for 小 is 小, Mandarin xiǎo, MC sjewX, OC *[s]ewʔ, gloss ‘small’; the opened source PDF was verified as the authors’ version 1.1 table, but browser extraction did not expose the specific 小 row. The value here is therefore reported as checked against the provided local row, not as an independently extracted online row.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"reconstruction_reference_and_local_row\",\n        \"url\": \"https://sites.lsa.umich.edu/ocbaxtersagart/wp-content/uploads/sites/1415/2025/03/BaxterSagartOCbyRadStr2014-09-20.pdf\",\n        \"title\": \"BaxterSagartOCbyRadStr2014-09-20\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-b1e6b91540b7c6134706\",\n        \"source\": \"Chinese University of Hong Kong, Multi-function Chinese Character Database\",\n        \"field\": \"雀 entry: component roles\",\n        \"text\": \"The database describes 小 in 雀 as both contributing the sense ‘small bird’ and functioning as a sound element. This is evidence for a phonetic role of 小 in that compound, but it does not establish that sand was the original object represented by 小. No comparison of 雀’s and 小’s readings in one reconstructed system was verified in this research.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"雀\",\n        \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n        \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-a6339f9c0072cd12d52a\",\n        \"source\": \"Unicode Consortium, Unihan Database Lookup\",\n        \"field\": \"Unihan lookup instructions and database scope\",\n        \"text\": \"The official page says the lookup interface provides property data for individual ideographs, including readings, and that data are based on Unicode 18.0.0. The exact 小 record could not be accessed through the required per-character endpoint. The supplied local Unihan_Readings.txt row for 小 gives kMandarin xiǎo; it is cited here as a local row check, not as externally verified character-specific Unicode evidence.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"official_database_documentation_and_local_row\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.unicode.org/charts/unihan.html\",\n        \"title\": \"Unihan Database Lookup\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-220d6fa8a217b3555938\",\n        \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n        \"field\": \"構形初義; 甲骨文用例; 金文用例\",\n        \"text\": \"The database records two competing origin analyses: three dots representing smallness, attributed to Shang Chengzuo and Yu Xingwu; or 小 as an early graph of 沙 depicting fine sand, attributed to Ma Xulun. It says 小 and 少 were one graph before differentiation. It cites oracle-bone 小雨 (《粹》1004), 小食 for afternoon, 小采 for dusk, bronze 小鼎, and 小子/小臣 for young nobles or lower officials. It gives no absolute dates for the cited artifacts or semantic developments.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"paleographic_and_historical_dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n        \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-a036255ebabd78a9e34e\",\n        \"source\": \"Academia Sinica, Character Database\",\n        \"field\": \"字形演變\",\n        \"text\": \"The page labels oracle-bone, bronze, small-seal and Shuowen stages. It asserts that the earlier marks depict scattered fine sand grains and says the middle dot in small-seal changed into a vertical stroke separating the other two. This is one source's analysis; the marks do not independently identify sand.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n        \"title\": \"漢字「小」：字形演變\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-eca33181dc16b0f2f777\",\n        \"source\": \"Wikimedia Commons\",\n        \"field\": \"Summary; original file; Licensing\",\n        \"text\": \"The inspected File page identifies 小-seal.svg as a modern vector depiction of 小 in Shuowen seal-script style and links its original image. The page states public-domain dedication for the representation, alongside CC0 information. This is a modern redraw, not an ancient artifact photograph.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"image_provenance_and_rights\",\n        \"url\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%B0%8F-seal.svg\",\n        \"title\": \"File:小-seal.svg\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-f6f7d68f09a02c854d24\",\n        \"source\": \"Academia Sinica, Character Database\",\n        \"field\": \"智財權聲明\",\n        \"text\": \"The inspected rights notice reserves intellectual property in the site's content and limits use absent a separate agreement; it does not provide CC0 reuse terms. Accordingly, its page is used as linked evidence, not as an image asset.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"rights_notice\",\n        \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/copyright.jsp\",\n        \"title\": \"智財權聲明\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-2829f816c26a5d71ec70\",\n        \"source\": \"Unicode Consortium, Unihan Database Lookup\",\n        \"field\": \"Per-character Unihan record\",\n        \"text\": \"The required individual record endpoint for 小 could not be opened in this run (internal fetch error). The supplied local Unihan row records kMandarin xiǎo, but is local data and is not independently verified here as a character-specific external record.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"access_failure_and_local_row_note\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5C0F\",\n        \"title\": \"Unihan Database Lookup\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-253281f9589a65c2d2a6\",\n        \"source\": \"Repository supplied local_primary_readings\",\n        \"field\": \"sources/unihan/Unihan_Readings.txt; kMandarin rows\",\n        \"text\": \"Supplied exact local rows: 小 xiǎo; 少 shǎo; 雀 què. These are current Mandarin metadata only, not evidence of ancient phonetic relationships. Their official individual Unihan click-through records for 小, 少, and 雀 were not verified as accessible in this run.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小; 少; 雀\",\n        \"kind\": \"local_reading_rows\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5C0F\",\n        \"title\": \"Unihan individual character lookup (endpoint unavailable)\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-af8f4361c990e6a92f5e\",\n        \"source\": \"Repository supplied local_primary_readings\",\n        \"field\": \"sources/baxter-sagart/baxtersagart.tsv; Baxter–Sagart 2014 rows\",\n        \"text\": \"Exact supplied rows: 小 xiǎo, MC sjewX, OC *[s]ewʔ (‘small’); 少 shǎo MC syewX OC *[s.t]ewʔ (‘few’) and shào MC syewH OC *[s-t]ewʔ-s (‘young’); 雀 què MC tsjak OC *[ts]ewk (‘sparrow’). These are Baxter–Sagart 2014 table notations, checked as local rows. The *[s]ewʔ and *[ts]ewk forms do not support an obvious rhyme match for a proposed 小→雀 sound role in that system; CUHK's component-role assertion can be reported as source-attributed, without treating the local forms as proof of a sound change.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小; 少; 雀\",\n        \"kind\": \"local_reconstruction_rows\",\n        \"url\": \"https://sites.lsa.umich.edu/ocbaxtersagart/wp-content/uploads/sites/1415/2025/03/BaxterSagartOCbyRadStr2014-09-20.pdf\",\n        \"title\": \"BaxterSagartOCbyRadStr2014-09-20 (version 1.1)\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-dd1f049d3ded734931ba\",\n        \"source\": \"李學勤主編,《字源》, 天津古籍出版社／遼寧人民出版社, 2012\",\n        \"field\": \"小 headword; PDF p. 76, printed p. 64; scanned headword and continuation checked on PDF p. 77, printed p. 65\",\n        \"text\": \"The scanned entry identifies 小 as pictographic and interprets its marks as tiny grains of dust or sand, calling it an early graph of 沙; it says the graph was extended to mean ‘small,’ opposite 大, and gives that sense in oracle-bone and bronze inscriptions. It cites 《粹》1004 for 小雨, then describes extensions to low status, contempt, and youth. It says the current form was corrupted in bronze inscriptions and treats Shuowen’s 八-plus-丨 account as an explanation of that altered form. The adjacent 少 entry says 小 and 少 were originally one graph, with similar use in oracle-bone texts, and later differentiated; its explanation continues onto printed p. 65. Direct scan inspection confirms the cited headword and passage. Forms checked against pixels: 小, 少, 沙, 八, 丨, 大, and the text’s citation 《粹》1004. The scan supports what this author asserts; it does not settle the disputed sand-grain interpretation.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"directly_inspected_book_scan\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.worldcat.org/search?q=9787552800692\",\n        \"title\": \"《字源》 (2012), PDF pp. 76–77; printed pp. 64–65\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-803fd94611bb57f92df9\",\n        \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n        \"field\": \"小: formation, early use and adjacent 少 entry\",\n        \"text\": \"The database reports two analyses of 小’s early marks: abstract dots for smallness, attributed to 商承祚 and 于省吾, or an early graph of 沙 depicting fine grains, attributed to 馬敘倫. It also describes 小 and 少 as an originally shared graph. Its examples include oracle-bone 小雨, time expressions 小食 and 小采, and bronze 小鼎, 小子 and 小臣. The page provides no absolute dates for these cited artifacts or usages, so it cannot alone establish a chronology among the senses.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"paleographic_and_historical_dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n        \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-5385acd88b51f476d32e\",\n        \"source\": \"金真姬,《常用漢字二百字探源》\",\n        \"field\": \"小, 字形探源／字義探源, PDF pp. 20–21; printed pp. 26–27\",\n        \"text\": \"The inspected entry reports disagreement about what the three dots represent, including raindrops, scattered objects or fine smallness. It favors an abstract indication of smallness and says later lengthened dots prompted Shuowen’s 八-plus-丨 analysis, which it rejects as based on the altered form. It cites oracle-bone 小雨, 小風 and 小牢 as uses for ‘small.’ This supports a competing scholarly account, not a settled referent for the dots.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"scholarly_reference\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.yjcn.nl/wp/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/%E5%B8%B8%E7用漢字二百字探源%EF%BC%88金真姬%EF%BC%89.pdf\",\n        \"title\": \"《常用漢字二百字探源》, PDF pp. 20–21\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-5ac63eb9bb056d4dc7cb\",\n        \"source\": \"中央研究院, Academia Sinica Character Database\",\n        \"field\": \"少 字形演變\",\n        \"text\": \"The page states that 少 and 小 were originally one graph depicting fine sand grains, with ‘small’ as the original meaning; it says the lower dot of 少 became a diagonal stroke in bronze inscriptions, distinguishing it from 小. This is an explicit shared-origin analysis, while other consulted sources retain competing analyses of 小’s dots.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"少\",\n        \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10271\",\n        \"title\": \"漢字「少」：字形演變\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-b8ded469510aa9455741\",\n        \"source\": \"李學勤主編,《字源》\",\n        \"field\": \"小 headword; PDF p. 76, printed p. 64; continuation PDF p. 77, printed p. 65\",\n        \"text\": \"The inspected entry calls 小 pictographic, interpreting its marks as tiny dust or sand particles and describing 小 as an early graph of 沙. It says the graph extended to mean ‘small,’ opposite 大, and reports that sense in oracle-bone and bronze inscriptions, citing 《粹》1004 for 小雨. It describes later extensions to low status, contempt and youth. It says the graph had become corrupted in bronze inscriptions and treats Shuowen’s 八-plus-丨 account as an explanation of that altered form. The adjacent 少 entry says 小 and 少 were originally one graph, used similarly in oracle-bone texts, and later differentiated; its account continues on printed p. 65. Both attached page images were inspected. Forms checked against scan pixels: 小, 少, 沙, 八, 丨, 大, and 《粹》1004. This verifies what this author claims, not the disputed sand-grain interpretation.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"directly_inspected_book_scan\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.worldcat.org/search?q=9787552800692\",\n        \"title\": \"《字源》, 李學勤主編, 天津古籍出版社／遼寧人民出版社, 2012, PDF pp. 76–77; printed pp. 64–65\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-cfcd778e20a67d7860ec\",\n        \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n        \"field\": \"小 formation, early uses and adjacent 少, 沙 and 雀 records\",\n        \"text\": \"The database reports competing interpretations of 小’s early marks: abstract dots for smallness, attributed to 商承祚 and 于省吾, or an early graph of 沙 depicting fine grains, attributed to 馬敍倫. It says 小 and 少 were one graph before differentiation, and that oracle-bone forms could use four dots for 小/少. It reports 小雨, 小食 (afternoon), 小采 (dusk), and bronze 小鼎, 小子 and 小臣, without absolute dates for the cited artifacts or semantic developments. Its 沙 entry discusses several analyses of 沙 forms; thus the page does not establish that 沙 was borrowed phonetically from 小. Its 雀 entry says 小 contributes both ‘small bird’ and sound, while separately reporting varied early uses and graphic forms.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小; 少; 沙; 雀\",\n        \"kind\": \"paleographic_and_historical_dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n        \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-4029d7e014bdb7910f42\",\n        \"source\": \"中央研究院, Academia Sinica Character Database\",\n        \"field\": \"小 字形演變\",\n        \"text\": \"The page labels oracle-bone, bronze, small-seal and Shuowen forms. It interprets the earlier marks as tiny sand grains scattered around, expressing smallness, and says the middle dot in small-seal script became a vertical stroke separating the two side marks. This is one source’s interpretation, not independent proof of the depicted referent.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n        \"title\": \"漢字「小」：字形演變\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-fe9ea9767e1da9fa626c\",\n        \"source\": \"教育部《異體字字典》, Taiwan Ministry of Education\",\n        \"field\": \"說文釋形; 釋義\",\n        \"text\": \"The dictionary preserves Xu Shen’s historical account: 小 means ‘the subtle/small among things’ and is analyzed as 八 and 丨, ‘seen and divided.’ It lists modern senses including small, make smaller, brief, young, lower-ranked, humble self-reference, slight degree and despise, with citations, but does not establish a chronological order among them.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?educode=A01068&powerMode=2\",\n        \"title\": \"教育部《異體字字典》：小\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-9cae30a34adfac4e5d42\",\n        \"source\": \"Nohara, “The reconstruction of the word shao (少) in Old Chinese Phonology”\",\n        \"field\": \"少 and 小 sound relationship; discussion and reconstruction comparison, pp. 2–6, 16\",\n        \"text\": \"The inspected study summarizes two positions on the proposed sound relationship around 少: Zhengzhang and Pan allow relationships among 少, 小 and related forms through reconstructed nasal initials; Schuessler and Baxter–Sagart reject a 少–小 phonetic-series relationship, with Schuessler treating 小 as semantic rather than phonetic in the cited discussion. The study also documents that early spellings 少 and 小 can both represent the words ‘small’ and ‘few’ in some oracle-bone, bronze and Warring States materials, with orthographic practice differing across regions and periods. This supports caution about inferring a phonetic relation from shared early spelling or present form alone.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"少; 小\",\n        \"kind\": \"scholarly_study\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/339973841_The_reconstruction_of_the_word_shao_shao_in_Old_Chinese_Phonology_shaonoshangguyinnitsuite\",\n        \"title\": \"「少」の上古音について／The reconstruction of the word shao (少) in Old Chinese Phonology\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-142dfc94245bc8e052bc\",\n        \"source\": \"Baxter and Sagart, Old Chinese reconstruction version 1.1\",\n        \"field\": \"Search result for author-hosted reconstruction table; PDF could not be opened in this invocation\",\n        \"text\": \"Search surfaced the authors’ version 1.1 table PDF, but the browser failed to open it. No specific 小, 少, 沙 or 雀 row was independently inspected in this invocation, so no table readings are asserted here.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小; 少; 沙; 雀\",\n        \"kind\": \"access_failure\",\n        \"url\": \"https://ocbaxtersagart.lsait.lsa.umich.edu/BaxterSagartOCbyMandarinMC2014-09-20.pdf\",\n        \"title\": \"Baxter-Sagart Old Chinese reconstruction, version 1.1\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-46ffd93eb016aa392f31\",\n        \"source\": \"李學勤主編,《字源》, 天津古籍出版社／遼寧人民出版社, 2012, ISBN 9787552800692\",\n        \"field\": \"小 headword; PDF p. 76, printed p. 64\",\n        \"text\": \"The entry calls 小 pictographic and interprets its marks as tiny dust or sand particles, an early graph of 沙. It says the graph was extended to mean ‘small,’ opposite 大, and cites oracle-bone and bronze uses, including 《粹》1004 小雨. It also describes extensions to low status, contempt and youth, and says the bronze form had become corrupted, prompting Shuowen’s 八-plus-丨 explanation. Both attached page images were inspected; the printed headword, cited forms 小, 沙, 大, 八, 丨 and 《粹》1004 are legible. This verifies the author’s account, not the disputed sand interpretation.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"directly_inspected_book_scan\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.worldcat.org/search?q=9787552800692\",\n        \"title\": \"《字源》, 李學勤主編, 2012, PDF p. 76; printed p. 64\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-c673b3b25eff702eb8d9\",\n        \"source\": \"李學勤主編,《字源》, 天津古籍出版社／遼寧人民出版社, 2012, ISBN 9787552800692\",\n        \"field\": \"Adjacent 少 entry; PDF p. 76 and continuation p. 77, printed pp. 64–65\",\n        \"text\": \"The adjacent 少 entry says 小 and 少 were originally one graph and were used alike in oracle-bone texts, then differentiated; it describes 少’s final diagonal stroke as a distinguishing mark. The entry continues onto printed p. 65. Both source scans were inspected; the relevant 少 and 小 forms are legible. This is the book author’s graphic account, not proof of a historical sound relationship.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"少; 小\",\n        \"kind\": \"directly_inspected_book_scan\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.worldcat.org/search?q=9787552800692\",\n        \"title\": \"《字源》, 李學勤主編, 2012, PDF pp. 76–77; printed pp. 64–65\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-047697228b315d31e79e\",\n        \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n        \"field\": \"小, 少 and 沙 records: formation, cited uses and graph components\",\n        \"text\": \"The 小 record presents two analyses of its early marks: abstract dots for smallness, attributed to 商承祚 and 于省吾, or an early graph of 沙 depicting fine sand grains, attributed to 馬敍倫. It reports 小雨, 小食 as an afternoon expression, 小采 as a dusk expression, and bronze uses including 小鼎, 小子 and 小臣, without absolute artifact dates. Its 少 record says early forms could overlap and that three-dot and four-dot spellings later distinguished 小 and 少. The 沙 account reports competing analyses of bronze uses, so the cited pages do not establish a phonetic borrowing of 沙 from 小.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小; 少; 沙\",\n        \"kind\": \"paleographic_and_historical_dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n        \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-0ec345d60e9fc6dc0872\",\n        \"source\": \"中央研究院, Academia Sinica Character Database\",\n        \"field\": \"少 字形演變\",\n        \"text\": \"The database asserts that 少 and 小 were originally one graph depicting fine sand grains, with ‘small’ as the original meaning, and says the lowest dot of 少 became a diagonal stroke in bronze inscriptions. This supports that interpretation as a source-attributed account; CUHK presents competing analyses of 小’s marks.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"少\",\n        \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10271\",\n        \"title\": \"漢字「少」：字形演變\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-1fc728b859bc4669b67d\",\n        \"source\": \"中央研究院, Academia Sinica Character Database\",\n        \"field\": \"小 字形演變\",\n        \"text\": \"The page labels oracle-bone, bronze, small-seal and Shuowen forms. It interprets the earlier marks as scattered fine sand grains expressing smallness and says the middle dot became a vertical stroke separating the two side marks in small-seal script. This is the database’s interpretation, not independent proof of the marks’ referent.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"小\",\n        \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n        \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n        \"title\": \"漢字「小」：字形演變\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"X-1b31b87c8aa5370dbe65\",\n        \"source\": \"Masaki Nohara, “The reconstruction of the word shao (少) in Old Chinese Phonology,” 中国語学 262 (2015), pp. 57–75\",\n        \"field\": \"少–小 phonetic relationship and early orthographic usage, especially PDF pp. 59–65\",\n        \"text\": \"Nohara reviews competing Old Chinese analyses. Zhengzhang and Pan allow links among 少, 小 and related forms via proposed nasal initials, while Schuessler and Baxter–Sagart reject a 少–小 phonetic-series relation in the discussion Nohara cites. Nohara argues that excavated-text spelling and sound evidence do not warrant treating the early graphic overlap as proof of a phonetic relationship. The paper also documents that 少 and 小 spellings could represent both ‘few’ and ‘small’ in some early materials, with regional and period differences.\",\n        \"record_character\": \"少; 小\",\n        \"kind\": \"scholarly_study\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/chuugokugogaku/2015/262/2015_57/_pdf\",\n        \"title\": \"「少」の上古音について／The reconstruction of the word shao (少) in Old Chinese Phonology\",\n        \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"context\": {\n      \"provenance\": \"Base evidence consists of imported local JSONL excerpts. Source names identify upstream datasets; extraction may lose sense and language boundaries. Further external evidence and research activity are documented separately in the dossier.\",\n      \"editorial_rules\": [\n        \"Write about the character's graphic history; distinguish it from the history of a spoken word.\",\n        \"Separate historical explanation from mnemonics. Do not infer history from modern shapes or readings.\",\n        \"Sources may repeat one another. A source count is not independent corroboration.\",\n        \"Treat Shuowen as a historical account, not automatic confirmation. Its generated English glosses are excluded.\",\n        \"Unrelated word senses may appear in Wiktionary excerpts. Do not merge them into a character origin.\",\n        \"Related-character evidence retains its record_character. Do not silently transfer a traditional form's components to a simplified form.\",\n        \"No glyph image has been visually inspected in this packet. Do not claim to have inspected one.\",\n        \"Explain missing evidence explicitly, especially for Japanese-created characters. A Chinese spelling pronunciation is not evidence for a Japanese origin.\"\n      ],\n      \"unverified_pipeline_metadata\": {\n        \"formation_type\": \"ideographic\",\n        \"formation_type_conflict\": {\n          \"makemeahanzi\": \"ideographic\",\n          \"dong_chinese\": \"other\",\n          \"shuowen_jiezi\": \"ideographic\",\n          \"wiktionary\": \"pictographic\"\n        },\n        \"formation_details\": null,\n        \"variants\": null\n      }\n    },\n    \"external_research\": {\n      \"search_audit\": [\n        {\n          \"query\": \"小 character oracle bone bronze inscriptions etymology Shuowen paleography; 小 說文 甲骨文 金文 字形 演變 小 字源; site:zi.tools 小 paleography bronze oracle bone 小; 小 少 relation Old Chinese Schuessler 2007\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n            \"https://scholarworks.iu.edu/dspace/items/b5a7377f-6b01-4704-a136-6b40a4d04078\",\n            \"https://www.guoxuedashi.com/zixing/yanbian/3081ht/\",\n            \"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%E5%B0%8F\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Opened Academia Sinica’s 小 evolution page and Wiktionary entry. Guoxuedashi result was later blocked by a verification page. Search results surfaced but did not establish the cited secondary Schuessler analysis.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"site:unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5C0F 小 kMandarin; site:ocbaxtersagart.lsait.lsa.umich.edu 小 沙 Old Chinese Baxter Sagart 2014; 小 最早 用例 甲骨文 小 大 說文 字義 殷周\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n            \"https://xiaoxue.iis.sinica.edu.tw/jiaguwen\",\n            \"https://www.zdic.net/hans/%E5%B0%8F\",\n            \"https://ctext.org/dictionary.pl?if=gb&rad=42\",\n            \"https://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?educode=A01068&powerMode=2\",\n            \"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=%E5%B0%8F\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Opened CUHK, Taiwan Ministry of Education and Academia Sinica pages. The requested Unihan endpoint returned an internal fetch error. CUHK provided early usage examples and competing graphic analyses.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"site:unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5C0F; Unihan 小 U+5C0F kMandarin xiǎo Unicode; \\\"小雨\\\" \\\"《粹》1004\\\" 甲骨\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://unicode.org/faq/han_cjk.html\",\n            \"https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr38/tr38-3.html\",\n            \"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%E5%B0%8F\",\n            \"https://www.unicode.org/charts/unihan.html\",\n            \"https://www.yjcn.nl/wp/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/%E5%B8%B8%E7%94%A8%E6%BC%A2%E5%AD%97%E4%BA%8C%E7%99%BE%E5%AD%97%E6%8E%A2%E6%BA%90%EF%BC%88%E9%87%91%E7%9C%9F%E5%A7%AC%EF%BC%89.pdf\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Unicode’s individual-record endpoint remained inaccessible. Official Unicode documentation and lookup page were opened; the detailed PDF was opened and supplied paleographic and oracle-bone usage evidence.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"site:ocbaxtersagart.lsait.lsa.umich.edu \\\"小\\\" \\\"沙\\\" *[s]ew; Baxter Sagart 2014 Old Chinese 小 沙 reconstruction; Chinese etymology 小 沙 original character paleography 马叙伦 小 少\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://academic.oup.com/book/26638\",\n            \"https://sites.lsa.umich.edu/ocbaxtersagart/\",\n            \"https://sites.lsa.umich.edu/ocbaxtersagart/wp-content/uploads/sites/1415/2025/03/BaxterSagartOCbyRadStr2014-09-20.pdf\",\n            \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n            \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10271\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Opened the author-hosted Baxter–Sagart table PDF and Academia Sinica 少 page. Reconstruction systems differ: Baxter–Sagart *[s]ewʔ and Zhengzhang *smewʔ for 小; the primary-search results did not establish a phonetic borrowing of 沙 from 小 or the original pronunciation of a depicted sand object.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"小 oracle bone bronze character formation three dots sand grains 說文 字形演變\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n            \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n            \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%B0%8F-seal.svg\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Inspected CUHK and Academia Sinica character-specific pages, plus the exact Commons file page. CUHK reports rival accounts of the dots and early usages; Academia Sinica supports its own sand-grain account and description of the seal-form change. Commons identifies the selected seal glyph as a modern redraw with reuse information.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"site:humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf 小 甲骨文 小雨 小 少\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Opened page and inspected relevant lines describing disputed formation, early examples, and 小–少 relation.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"site:commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File 小-seal.svg\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%B0%8F-seal.svg\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Exact Commons file page opened. Verified graph identity, original-file link, modern redraw status and rights statement.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"Academia Sinica Xiaoxuetang 小 字形演變 小學堂 glyph CC0 image; site:unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5C0F\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://xiaoxue.iis.sinica.edu.tw/yanbian/Home/Home\",\n            \"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5C0F\",\n            \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/copyright.jsp\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Xiaoxuetang landing page and Character Database rights notice inspected; no 小-specific Xiaoxuetang glyph record was retrieved. The Unicode per-character endpoint returned an internal fetch error.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"小 字形 甲骨文 金文 三点 沙 小 少 字源\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n            \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10271\",\n            \"https://www.yjcn.nl/wp/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/%E5%B8%B8%E7用漢字二百字探源%EF%BC%88金真姬%EF%BC%89.pdf\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Opened CUHK’s 小 record, Academia Sinica’s 少 evolution page, and the PDF entry for 小. These sources support competing interpretations of 小’s early marks and report a relationship between 小 and 少.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"小 少 甲骨文 同字 分化 說文 小 甲骨 用例 CUHK Character database\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Opened the CUHK page and checked its 小 formation and early-use account, the linked 少 discussion, and its 沙 and 雀 component notes.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"小 字形演變 甲骨文 少 sand grains smallness Academia Sinica; site:humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf 小 甲骨文 小雨 小 少; 小 Shuowen oracle bone character origin dots sand grains scholarly\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n            \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n            \"https://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?educode=A01068&powerMode=2\",\n            \"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%E5%B0%8F\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Opened the Sinica, CUHK and Taiwan Ministry of Education pages and inspected their character-specific content. They confirm competing accounts of the earliest marks, the historical Shuowen analysis, cited early uses and the 小–少 discussion. Wiktionary opened but was not used as evidence.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"site:ocbaxtersagart.lsait.lsa.umich.edu 小 少 沙 Baxter Sagart table; Old Chinese 小 少 沙 reconstruction Zhengzhang Baxter Sagart sound relationship; 小 少 原始字 甲骨文 字形 分化 郭沫若 商承祚 于省吾\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://academic.oup.com/book/26638\",\n            \"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/339973841_The_reconstruction_of_the_word_shao_shao_in_Old_Chinese_Phonology_shaonoshanggitsunitesh?\",\n            \"https://ocbaxtersagart.lsait.lsa.umich.edu/BaxterSagartOCbyMandarinMC2014-09-20.pdf\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Search found Baxter and Sagart’s version 1.1 table, but opening it returned an internal error; no table row was verified. Opened Nohara’s study and inspected its discussion of competing phonetic analyses and early orthographic usage for 少 and 小. The Oxford page verified the book’s publication metadata only and was not used for character claims.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"Live scan inspection of supplied 字源 PDF pages 76–77 / printed pp. 64–65\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://www.worldcat.org/search?q=9787552800692\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Inspected both supplied original scan images directly. PDF p. 76 contains the 小 headword; p. 77 continues its adjacent 少 discussion. Scan readings were checked for 小, 少, 沙, 八, 丨, 大 and 《粹》1004. No OCR error was identified in the cited 小 passage. The WorldCat page could not be opened; bibliographic details are from the supplied source registration, not the catalogue.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"小 oracle bone bronze character etymology academic paleography three dots sand grains 沙 小 少; site:humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf 小 少 甲骨文 沙 字源; 小 少 Old Chinese phonological relationship Nohara\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n            \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%91\",\n            \"https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/chuugokugogaku/2015/262/2015_57/_article/-char/ja\",\n            \"https://waseda.repo.nii.ac.jp/record/64927/files/ChugokuBungakuKenkyu_44_14.pdf\",\n            \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n            \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10271\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Search found the CUHK character records, Academia Sinica evolution pages and Nohara’s study. Opened and inspected the CUHK 小 and 少 records, both Sinica pages, and the J-STAGE PDF. The J-STAGE article landing page failed to open, but the PDF opened and its discussion was inspected.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"漢語多功能字庫 小 字形演變 少 字源 沙 商承祚 于省吾 馬敘倫\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n            \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10271\",\n            \"https://www.hiemalis.org/~acy/mnc/2679131gc1j.html\",\n            \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/ancient.php?start=920\",\n            \"https://www.ch.ntnu.edu.tw/SIS/show_paper_detail.php?issue_id=42&paper_id=378&periodicalsDir=DESC&periodicalsOrder=Sorter_issue_ch&periodicalsPage=7\",\n            \"https://www.chnmuseum.cn/portals/0/web/zt/20191022jiagu/\",\n            \"https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/chuugokugogaku/2015/262/2015_57/_pdf\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"A targeted follow-up surfaced the same CUHK and Sinica claims plus general bibliographic/context pages. The character-specific pages and J-STAGE PDF were inspected; the other results were not used as evidence.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"Live inspection of supplied 字源 scans, PDF pp. 76–77 / printed pp. 64–65\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://www.worldcat.org/search?q=9787552800692\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Opened the supplied original-resolution scan images for PDF pages 76 and 77 and inspected targeted crops. Confirmed the 小 headword and passage on page 76 and the adjacent 少 continuation context on page 77. Checked the printed forms 小, 少, 沙, 大, 八, 丨 and citation 《粹》1004 against the pixels. No OCR correction was identified in the cited passage. The WorldCat URL was not opened; bibliographic metadata came from the supplied source registration.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"gaps\": [\n        \"The small-sand-grain depiction / 小 as an early graph of 沙 analysis is disputed; sources also analyze the dots as abstract marks for smallness, and the depicted referent is not independently established.\",\n        \"The graph’s oracle-bone use meaning ‘small’ is reported with specific inscription citation 《粹》1004, but this research did not inspect a facsimile or establish an absolute date for that artifact. CUHK also reports separate time terms 小食 and 小采 without dates or a demonstrated semantic bridge from ‘small.’\",\n        \"No evidence here establishes that 沙 was borrowed phonetically using a word name for the depicted grains. Treating 小 as the source graph of 沙 remains an attributed proposal, not a proven sound loan; the sand-object name and pronunciation are unrecoverable from the consulted evidence.\",\n        \"The 小–少 graphic relationship is supported by sources describing an original shared graph and later differentiation, while the specific sand-grain analysis remains contested. Wiktionary reports an exceptional Middle Chinese s-/ɕ- alternation in a proposed word-family relationship, but the primary sources accessed here do not resolve the lexical relationship or independently document Schuessler’s argument.\",\n        \"No absolute dates were recovered for the cited bronze examples or their semantic extensions. Do not use modern dictionary gloss ordering as a chronology.\",\n        \"The character-specific official Unicode Unihan page https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5C0F repeatedly failed to open. Current kMandarin xiǎo was checked in the supplied local source row; no separately inspectable official per-character URL could be verified.\",\n        \"For 雀, CUHK asserts 小 is a phonetic component, but a same-system reconstruction comparison for both 雀 and 小 was not completed. The local Baxter–Sagart file does not substitute for inspection of both exact rows, and the sound role should remain source-attributed rather than demonstrated here.\",\n        \"The local glyph candidates were not opened or visually inspected in this research; no claims are made from those files.\",\n        \"Whether the earliest dots depict grains of sand or are abstract marks for smallness remains disputed. No inspected evidence establishes the specific depicted object or a phonetic borrowing of 沙; the sand analysis is attributed to Ma Xulun, not demonstrated as a sound loan.\",\n        \"CUHK reports an oracle-bone usage 小雨 with the citation 《粹》1004, but this research did not inspect a facsimile or establish the artifact's absolute date. It reports time expressions and later bronze uses without dates or a demonstrated semantic bridge from ‘small.’\",\n        \"The 小–少 shared-graph and differentiation account is reported by CUHK, but the lexical and graphic details are not settled by the material inspected here.\",\n        \"CUHK reports 小 as a sound component in 雀. Local Baxter–Sagart rows are included for both graphs, but do not by themselves explain that source-attributed phonetic role; the individual character pages and a phonetic-history account were not independently verified.\",\n        \"The official Unicode individual-record endpoint for 小 returned an internal fetch error. Local reading rows are identified as local provenance, not externally confirmed records.\",\n        \"No Xiaoxuetang single-character form page or image was obtained in the inspected pages. The selected image is therefore the Commons modern seal-script redraw, not an ancient artifact image. The separate Sinica Character Database page states All Rights Reserved, so no image from that site is proposed.\",\n        \"字源’s claim that 小’s marks depict sand grains and that 小 was an early graph of 沙 is this author’s analysis; consulted references also support an abstract smallness-sign account. The original depicted referent remains unsettled. No inspected source establishes a phonetic borrowing of 沙 based on the name or pronunciation of depicted sand grains.\",\n        \"The 字源 entry reports oracle-bone 小雨 and other early meanings, but the underlying inscriptions were not inspected here; no absolute artifact dates or demonstrated semantic bridge for the time and status uses were established.\",\n        \"字源 PDF page 76 is printed p. 64; its continuation is PDF page 77, printed p. 65. Both scan images were directly inspected. No specific OCR correction was identified in the cited 小 passage.\",\n        \"The local reading row for 小 is current kMandarin metadata, not evidence about ancient sound relationships. The official individual Unicode Unihan record endpoint was not accessed in this research invocation.\",\n        \"The CUHK page attributes a sound role to 小 in 雀, but this invocation did not independently establish a historical sound relationship using inspected component and host readings in the same reconstruction system. Keep that role source-attributed and unresolved.\",\n        \"The earliest marks’ specific referent remains disputed: inspected sources present both abstract marks for smallness and fine sand grains. No inspected evidence establishes the sand object’s name or shows that 沙 was borrowed phonetically using that name.\",\n        \"The book’s cited oracle-bone 小雨 example was not checked against an inscription facsimile; no absolute artifact date was verified. The consulted sources report time and status uses without establishing their dates or semantic bridges from ‘small.’\",\n        \"Accounts support some early graphic and orthographic overlap between 小 and 少, but the specific development and lexical relationship remain contested. Nohara’s study reports competing phonological analyses; its ResearchGate page was inspected, but the underlying cited Schuessler and Baxter–Sagart pages were not independently opened here.\",\n        \"The official individual Unihan endpoint and the Baxter–Sagart table could not be inspected in this invocation. No current or reconstructed reading rows are newly asserted; local rows in the input remain local data and are not treated as external verification.\",\n        \"The 《字源》 scan backs the author’s analysis but does not settle it. No specific OCR correction was identified for the cited 小 passage. The WorldCat catalogue URL could not be opened; publication metadata were supplied in the input.\",\n        \"The earliest marks’ referent remains disputed: consulted accounts describe abstract marks for smallness or fine sand grains. No inspected evidence independently establishes the depicted object or a phonetic borrowing of 沙 based on its name.\",\n        \"The 《字源》 entry reports oracle-bone 小雨 with 《粹》1004, but no inscription facsimile or absolute artifact date was checked. The consulted sources report time and status uses without establishing their dates or semantic bridges from ‘small.’\",\n        \"The shared-graph and later differentiation account for 小 and 少 is reported by several references, but it does not itself establish a historical sound relationship. Nohara’s inspected study finds the phonetic connection unsupported by the evidence he examines; the broader lexical relationship remains unsettled.\",\n        \"CUHK reports 小 as a sound component in 雀. This research did not establish that role through an independent historical sound comparison, so it remains source-attributed.\",\n        \"The WorldCat catalogue URL was not inspected. Edition details are from the supplied source registration; the source scans themselves were directly inspected.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"glyph_research\": {\n      \"historical_glyphs\": {\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"小-seal\",\n            \"image_url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/%E5%B0%8F-seal.svg\",\n            \"source_url\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%B0%8F-seal.svg\",\n            \"source_title\": \"File:小-seal.svg\",\n            \"period\": \"Modern vector redraw of the Shuowen small-seal form; depicts an ancient script style, not a dated artifact\",\n            \"tradition\": \"Small seal script (小篆), Shuowen style\",\n            \"caption\": \"This modern redraw shows 小 in Shuowen small-seal style. The central dot has become a vertical stroke between two side marks; this later shape does not settle what the earlier marks represented.\",\n            \"alt\": \"Three black strokes: a long central vertical stroke between two shorter, slightly curved side strokes.\",\n            \"selection_reason\": \"It illustrates the seal-script form and the described graphic change while keeping the disputed interpretation of the earlier marks open.\",\n            \"rights\": \"Public-domain dedication for the modern vector representation; Commons page also records CC0 information.\",\n            \"rights_url\": \"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\",\n            \"evidence_ids\": [\n              \"X-21e5c27b88aea75dc33a\",\n              \"X-eca33181dc16b0f2f777\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"limitations\": [\n          {\n            \"text\": \"This is a modern redraw, not an ancient inscription image. The earlier marks are interpreted either as abstract signs of smallness or as fine sand grains, and their referent remains uncertain.\",\n            \"evidence_ids\": [\n              \"X-9337d44faa93154e5b08\",\n              \"X-2a90e282a2ff3f19511d\",\n              \"X-eca33181dc16b0f2f777\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"search_audit\": [\n        {\n          \"query\": \"小 oracle bone bronze character formation three dots sand grains 說文 字形演變\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n            \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n            \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%B0%8F-seal.svg\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Inspected CUHK and Academia Sinica character-specific pages, plus the exact Commons file page. CUHK reports rival accounts of the dots and early usages; Academia Sinica supports its own sand-grain account and description of the seal-form change. Commons identifies the selected seal glyph as a modern redraw with reuse information.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"site:humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf 小 甲骨文 小雨 小 少\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Opened page and inspected relevant lines describing disputed formation, early examples, and 小–少 relation.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"site:commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File 小-seal.svg\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%B0%8F-seal.svg\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Exact Commons file page opened. Verified graph identity, original-file link, modern redraw status and rights statement.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"query\": \"Academia Sinica Xiaoxuetang 小 字形演變 小學堂 glyph CC0 image; site:unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5C0F\",\n          \"urls\": [\n            \"https://xiaoxue.iis.sinica.edu.tw/yanbian/Home/Home\",\n            \"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5C0F\",\n            \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/copyright.jsp\"\n          ],\n          \"outcome\": \"Xiaoxuetang landing page and Character Database rights notice inspected; no 小-specific Xiaoxuetang glyph record was retrieved. The Unicode per-character endpoint returned an internal fetch error.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"gaps\": [\n        \"Whether the earliest dots depict grains of sand or are abstract marks for smallness remains disputed. No inspected evidence establishes the specific depicted object or a phonetic borrowing of 沙; the sand analysis is attributed to Ma Xulun, not demonstrated as a sound loan.\",\n        \"CUHK reports an oracle-bone usage 小雨 with the citation 《粹》1004, but this research did not inspect a facsimile or establish the artifact's absolute date. It reports time expressions and later bronze uses without dates or a demonstrated semantic bridge from ‘small.’\",\n        \"The 小–少 shared-graph and differentiation account is reported by CUHK, but the lexical and graphic details are not settled by the material inspected here.\",\n        \"CUHK reports 小 as a sound component in 雀. Local Baxter–Sagart rows are included for both graphs, but do not by themselves explain that source-attributed phonetic role; the individual character pages and a phonetic-history account were not independently verified.\",\n        \"The official Unicode individual-record endpoint for 小 returned an internal fetch error. Local reading rows are identified as local provenance, not externally confirmed records.\",\n        \"No Xiaoxuetang single-character form page or image was obtained in the inspected pages. The selected image is therefore the Commons modern seal-script redraw, not an ancient artifact image. The separate Sinica Character Database page states All Rights Reserved, so no image from that site is proposed.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"glyph_assets\": [\n      {\n        \"glyph_id\": \"小-seal\",\n        \"source_url\": \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/%E5%B0%8F-seal.svg\",\n        \"sha256\": \"61906767a952d4e4e1b965d4ce6a0537d34b4d25a72dd3fc731d37b4a4991ba0\",\n        \"mime_type\": \"image/svg+xml\",\n        \"path\": \"content/glyph-assets/61906767a952d4e4e1b965d4ce6a0537d34b4d25a72dd3fc731d37b4a4991ba0.svg\",\n        \"byte_length\": 1807\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"review\": {\n    \"status\": \"approved\",\n    \"article_hash\": \"5c727c033b6385ffc7d9e54131b8d8a906e83d2f64155b55a91de3865c66e513\",\n    \"dossier_hash\": \"9ff455f5b1ebb127e529019af426e952e152b2e9c5da335741b909dcd57938ae\",\n    \"reviews\": [\n      {\n        \"role\": \"factual\",\n        \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n        \"findings\": [],\n        \"article_hash\": \"5c727c033b6385ffc7d9e54131b8d8a906e83d2f64155b55a91de3865c66e513\",\n        \"dossier_hash\": \"9ff455f5b1ebb127e529019af426e952e152b2e9c5da335741b909dcd57938ae\",\n        \"reviewer\": \"gpt-6-luna:low:factual:01a0fe76-e24e-7580-96a1-2c0ea5ea4c68\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"readability\",\n        \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n        \"findings\": [],\n        \"article_hash\": \"5c727c033b6385ffc7d9e54131b8d8a906e83d2f64155b55a91de3865c66e513\",\n        \"dossier_hash\": \"9ff455f5b1ebb127e529019af426e952e152b2e9c5da335741b909dcd57938ae\",\n        \"reviewer\": \"gpt-6-luna:low:readability:01a0fe77-e6f3-74f2-b879-e6569b088612\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"character\": \"小\",\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E1\",\n      \"source\": \"makemeahanzi\",\n      \"field\": \"hanzi.etymology_notes[0]\",\n      \"text\": \"Dividing 八 by a line 亅\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E2\",\n      \"source\": \"dong_chinese\",\n      \"field\": \"hanzi.etymology_notes[1]\",\n      \"text\": \"Pictograph of three small dots, representing grains of sand or rice, to convey the meaning \\\"small\\\".\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E3\",\n      \"source\": \"shuowen_jiezi\",\n      \"field\": \"hanzi.etymology_notes[2]\",\n      \"text\": \"物之微也。从八，丨見而分之。凡小之屬皆从小。\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E4\",\n      \"source\": \"wiktionary\",\n      \"field\": \"hanzi.etymology_notes[3]\",\n      \"text\": \"Two possible interpretations:\\n* Ideogram (指事) – three small dots > small.\\n* Pictogram (象形) – three granules of sand – original character of 沙 (OC *sraːl, *sraːls) > small.\\nStarting from some bronze inscriptions, the dots have become elongated. Based on this form, Shuowen erroneously considers it to be an ideogrammic compound (會意 /会意): 八 (“to divide; to separate”) + 丨 (“small object”).\\nCompare with 少 (OC *hmjewʔ, *hmjews), represented by four dots in its oracle bone script form. Unrelated to the bottom part of 京, 示, 尞, 尗, and 原.\\nOften thought to be related to 少 (OC *hmjewʔ, *hmjews) (e.g. Wang, 1982), but Schuessler (2007) points out that the alternation between Middle Chinese /s-/ and /ɕ-/ within a word family is exceptional.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E5\",\n      \"source\": \"shuowen_jiezi\",\n      \"field\": \"hanzi.shuowen.explanation\",\n      \"text\": \"物之微也。从八，丨見而分之。凡小之屬皆从小。\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E6\",\n      \"source\": \"merged_record\",\n      \"field\": \"hanzi.definitions\",\n      \"text\": \"small, tiny, insignificant\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_metadata\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E7\",\n      \"source\": \"merged_record\",\n      \"field\": \"hanzi.readings\",\n      \"text\": \"{\\\"cantonese\\\": \\\"siu2\\\", \\\"japanese_kun\\\": \\\"CHIISAI KO O\\\", \\\"japanese_on\\\": \\\"SHOU\\\", \\\"korean\\\": \\\"SO\\\", \\\"mandarin\\\": \\\"xiǎo\\\", \\\"tang\\\": \\\"*siɛ̌u\\\", \\\"vietnamese\\\": \\\"tiểu\\\"}\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_metadata\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E8\",\n      \"source\": \"merged_record\",\n      \"field\": \"hanzi.historical_phonology\",\n      \"text\": \"[{\\\"gloss\\\": \\\"small\\\", \\\"gsr\\\": \\\"1149a\\\", \\\"middle_chinese\\\": \\\"sjewX\\\", \\\"old_chinese\\\": \\\"*[s]ewʔ\\\"}, {\\\"old_chinese_zhengzhang\\\": \\\"*smewʔ\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"zhengzhang_wikt\\\"}, {\\\"old_chinese_zhengzhang\\\": \\\"*smewʔ\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"zhengzhang_wikt\\\"}, {\\\"fanqie\\\": \\\"私兆\\\", \\\"middle_chinese_guangyun\\\": \\\"心開三宵上\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"guangyun\\\"}, {\\\"old_chinese_zhengzhang\\\": \\\"smewʔ\\\", \\\"rhyme_group\\\": \\\"宵\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"zhengzhang\\\"}]\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_metadata\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E9\",\n      \"source\": \"kanjidic2_via_build_kanji\",\n      \"field\": \"kanji.definition\",\n      \"text\": \"Little; Small\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_metadata\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E10\",\n      \"source\": \"kanjidic2_via_build_kanji\",\n      \"field\": \"kanji.readings\",\n      \"text\": \"{\\\"japanese_kun\\\": \\\"ちい.さい こ- お- さ-\\\", \\\"japanese_on\\\": \\\"ショウ\\\"}\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_metadata\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E11\",\n      \"source\": \"ids_analysis\",\n      \"field\": \"kanji.etymology_notes[4]\",\n      \"text\": \"Etymological analysis: 會意\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"imported_excerpt\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-874259a2b827e31d1455\",\n      \"source\": \"Academia Sinica, Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"小 字形演變\",\n      \"text\": \"The database identifies oracle-bone and bronze forms, and gives two possible interpretations of their marks: three small dots symbolizing smallness, or grains of sand scattered around. It says that in small-seal script the central dot became a vertical stroke separating the two others.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n      \"title\": \"漢字「小」：字形演變\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-21e5c27b88aea75dc33a\",\n      \"source\": \"Academia Sinica, Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"甲骨文、金文、小篆字形\",\n      \"text\": \"The page labels the displayed stages oracle bone, bronze, small-seal, and Shuowen. Its account describes the seal form as a graphic alteration of earlier dots; the shapes alone do not establish the identity of a depicted object.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n      \"title\": \"漢字「小」：字形演變\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-9337d44faa93154e5b08\",\n      \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n      \"field\": \"甲骨文及構形初義\",\n      \"text\": \"The database records competing analyses: three small dots signifying smallness, attributed to Shang Chengzuo and Yu Xingwu; or 小 as an early graph of 沙, depicting fine sand grains, attributed to Ma Xulun. It also says 小 and 少 were originally one graph and later differentiated.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n      \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-7c4ee97c98a3f9f753ae\",\n      \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n      \"field\": \"甲骨文詞例及金文用例\",\n      \"text\": \"It reports oracle-bone 小 meaning ‘small,’ citing 《粹》1004 小雨; it separately reports 小食 as an afternoon time expression and 小采 as an evening expression. For bronze inscriptions it gives 嬴霝德鼎 小鼎 and notes 小子 for young aristocratic sons and lower officials, and 小臣 for officials subordinate to rulers. The page supplies no absolute dates for these cited artifacts or semantic developments.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"historical_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n      \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-7098042d6576a6e2edc8\",\n      \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n      \"field\": \"少 entry, graphic and usage account\",\n      \"text\": \"It says oracle-bone forms of 小/少 could have four dots and were used in the same way; later the three-dot graph was used for 小 and four-dot form for 少. In bronze forms, the lowest dot of 少 extended into a diagonal stroke. The page cites bronze uses of 少 for ‘few’ and ‘young,’ and a later case where 少 is read as 小. This supports graphic differentiation and shared early use, but does not settle the more specific proposed sand-grain referent.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"historical_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n      \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-6a67a2eba00317f0db96\",\n      \"source\": \"Academia Sinica, Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"少 字形演變\",\n      \"text\": \"The database states that 少 and 小 were originally one graph depicting fine sand grains, with ‘small’ as the original meaning; in bronze inscriptions the bottom dot of 少 became a diagonal stroke, distinguishing it from 小. This is a clear assertion of the shared-origin analysis, while CUHK presents that relationship alongside competing accounts of 小’s earliest formation.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"少\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10271\",\n      \"title\": \"漢字「少」：字形演變\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-2a90e282a2ff3f19511d\",\n      \"source\": \"《常用漢字二百字探源》 (PDF), entry 小\",\n      \"field\": \"字形探源 and 字義探源, pp. 20–21\",\n      \"text\": \"The book lists oracle-bone and bronze examples and says both scripts write 小 with three dots. It reports disagreement over what the dots depict, including raindrops, scattered objects, or fine smallness; it judges an abstract indicator-of-smallness analysis plausible. It says later dots lengthened into lines and rejects Shuowen’s parsing of the seal form as 八 plus 丨 as an error based on the later shape. It cites oracle-bone examples 小雨, 小風, and 小牢 for the ‘small’ use. This provides another account of the dots and the alleged graphic reinterpretation, not independent proof that they depict sand.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"scholarly_reference\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.yjcn.nl/wp/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/%E5%B8%B8%E7%94%A8%E6%BC%A2%E5%AD%97%E4%BA%8C%E7%99%BE%E5%AD%97%E6%8E%A2%E6%BA%90%EF%BC%88%E9%87%91%E7%9C%9F%E5%A7%AC%EF%BC%89.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"常用漢字二百字探源\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-266b8f35d92e78d22ad7\",\n      \"source\": \"Ministry of Education, Taiwan, Dictionary of Chinese Character Variants\",\n      \"field\": \"說文釋形; 字樣說明; 釋義\",\n      \"text\": \"The dictionary reproduces Xu Shen’s analysis: 小 means ‘the subtle/small among things’ and is analyzed as 八 and 丨, ‘seen and divided.’ It preserves this as a historical dictionary account. Its modern senses include small in size or quantity, make smaller, briefly, young, low-ranking, and humble self-reference, with classical citations; the page does not establish a chronological order among those senses.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?educode=A01068&powerMode=2\",\n      \"title\": \"教育部《異體字字典》：小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-1ba7a1471a7e7d07ce0d\",\n      \"source\": \"Wiktionary, 小 entry (consulted for competing analysis and reconstruction display)\",\n      \"field\": \"Chinese Glyph origin; Middle Chinese and Old Chinese readings\",\n      \"text\": \"The entry presents both an indicator interpretation (three dots to mean small) and a pictorial sand-grain interpretation, the latter identifying 小 as an early graph of 沙. It labels the 八 plus 丨 analysis in Shuowen an erroneous interpretation of an altered seal form. Its displayed comparisons are Middle Chinese 小 sjewX, Baxter–Sagart Old Chinese *[s]ewʔ, and Zhengzhang *smewʔ. These are source-reported reconstructions, not interchangeable notations.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"dictionary_and_reconstruction_compilation\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%E5%B0%8F\",\n      \"title\": \"小 - Wiktionary\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-e79ea1cfe5b5aa959a40\",\n      \"source\": \"Baxter and Sagart, Old Chinese reconstruction version 1.1, 13 September 2014\",\n      \"field\": \"Reconstruction notation documentation\",\n      \"text\": \"The authors distinguish Middle Chinese transcription from reconstruction, explain that square brackets mark uncertain identity and parentheses uncertain presence, and identify the table as version 1.1. The locally supplied Baxter–Sagart row for 小 is 小, Mandarin xiǎo, MC sjewX, OC *[s]ewʔ, gloss ‘small’; the opened source PDF was verified as the authors’ version 1.1 table, but browser extraction did not expose the specific 小 row. The value here is therefore reported as checked against the provided local row, not as an independently extracted online row.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"reconstruction_reference_and_local_row\",\n      \"url\": \"https://sites.lsa.umich.edu/ocbaxtersagart/wp-content/uploads/sites/1415/2025/03/BaxterSagartOCbyRadStr2014-09-20.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"BaxterSagartOCbyRadStr2014-09-20\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-b1e6b91540b7c6134706\",\n      \"source\": \"Chinese University of Hong Kong, Multi-function Chinese Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"雀 entry: component roles\",\n      \"text\": \"The database describes 小 in 雀 as both contributing the sense ‘small bird’ and functioning as a sound element. This is evidence for a phonetic role of 小 in that compound, but it does not establish that sand was the original object represented by 小. No comparison of 雀’s and 小’s readings in one reconstructed system was verified in this research.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"雀\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n      \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-a6339f9c0072cd12d52a\",\n      \"source\": \"Unicode Consortium, Unihan Database Lookup\",\n      \"field\": \"Unihan lookup instructions and database scope\",\n      \"text\": \"The official page says the lookup interface provides property data for individual ideographs, including readings, and that data are based on Unicode 18.0.0. The exact 小 record could not be accessed through the required per-character endpoint. The supplied local Unihan_Readings.txt row for 小 gives kMandarin xiǎo; it is cited here as a local row check, not as externally verified character-specific Unicode evidence.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"official_database_documentation_and_local_row\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.unicode.org/charts/unihan.html\",\n      \"title\": \"Unihan Database Lookup\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-220d6fa8a217b3555938\",\n      \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n      \"field\": \"構形初義; 甲骨文用例; 金文用例\",\n      \"text\": \"The database records two competing origin analyses: three dots representing smallness, attributed to Shang Chengzuo and Yu Xingwu; or 小 as an early graph of 沙 depicting fine sand, attributed to Ma Xulun. It says 小 and 少 were one graph before differentiation. It cites oracle-bone 小雨 (《粹》1004), 小食 for afternoon, 小采 for dusk, bronze 小鼎, and 小子/小臣 for young nobles or lower officials. It gives no absolute dates for the cited artifacts or semantic developments.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_and_historical_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n      \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-a036255ebabd78a9e34e\",\n      \"source\": \"Academia Sinica, Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"字形演變\",\n      \"text\": \"The page labels oracle-bone, bronze, small-seal and Shuowen stages. It asserts that the earlier marks depict scattered fine sand grains and says the middle dot in small-seal changed into a vertical stroke separating the other two. This is one source's analysis; the marks do not independently identify sand.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n      \"title\": \"漢字「小」：字形演變\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-eca33181dc16b0f2f777\",\n      \"source\": \"Wikimedia Commons\",\n      \"field\": \"Summary; original file; Licensing\",\n      \"text\": \"The inspected File page identifies 小-seal.svg as a modern vector depiction of 小 in Shuowen seal-script style and links its original image. The page states public-domain dedication for the representation, alongside CC0 information. This is a modern redraw, not an ancient artifact photograph.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"image_provenance_and_rights\",\n      \"url\": \"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%B0%8F-seal.svg\",\n      \"title\": \"File:小-seal.svg\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-f6f7d68f09a02c854d24\",\n      \"source\": \"Academia Sinica, Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"智財權聲明\",\n      \"text\": \"The inspected rights notice reserves intellectual property in the site's content and limits use absent a separate agreement; it does not provide CC0 reuse terms. Accordingly, its page is used as linked evidence, not as an image asset.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"rights_notice\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/copyright.jsp\",\n      \"title\": \"智財權聲明\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-2829f816c26a5d71ec70\",\n      \"source\": \"Unicode Consortium, Unihan Database Lookup\",\n      \"field\": \"Per-character Unihan record\",\n      \"text\": \"The required individual record endpoint for 小 could not be opened in this run (internal fetch error). The supplied local Unihan row records kMandarin xiǎo, but is local data and is not independently verified here as a character-specific external record.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"access_failure_and_local_row_note\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5C0F\",\n      \"title\": \"Unihan Database Lookup\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-253281f9589a65c2d2a6\",\n      \"source\": \"Repository supplied local_primary_readings\",\n      \"field\": \"sources/unihan/Unihan_Readings.txt; kMandarin rows\",\n      \"text\": \"Supplied exact local rows: 小 xiǎo; 少 shǎo; 雀 què. These are current Mandarin metadata only, not evidence of ancient phonetic relationships. Their official individual Unihan click-through records for 小, 少, and 雀 were not verified as accessible in this run.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小; 少; 雀\",\n      \"kind\": \"local_reading_rows\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5C0F\",\n      \"title\": \"Unihan individual character lookup (endpoint unavailable)\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-af8f4361c990e6a92f5e\",\n      \"source\": \"Repository supplied local_primary_readings\",\n      \"field\": \"sources/baxter-sagart/baxtersagart.tsv; Baxter–Sagart 2014 rows\",\n      \"text\": \"Exact supplied rows: 小 xiǎo, MC sjewX, OC *[s]ewʔ (‘small’); 少 shǎo MC syewX OC *[s.t]ewʔ (‘few’) and shào MC syewH OC *[s-t]ewʔ-s (‘young’); 雀 què MC tsjak OC *[ts]ewk (‘sparrow’). These are Baxter–Sagart 2014 table notations, checked as local rows. The *[s]ewʔ and *[ts]ewk forms do not support an obvious rhyme match for a proposed 小→雀 sound role in that system; CUHK's component-role assertion can be reported as source-attributed, without treating the local forms as proof of a sound change.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小; 少; 雀\",\n      \"kind\": \"local_reconstruction_rows\",\n      \"url\": \"https://sites.lsa.umich.edu/ocbaxtersagart/wp-content/uploads/sites/1415/2025/03/BaxterSagartOCbyRadStr2014-09-20.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"BaxterSagartOCbyRadStr2014-09-20 (version 1.1)\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-09-27\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-dd1f049d3ded734931ba\",\n      \"source\": \"李學勤主編,《字源》, 天津古籍出版社／遼寧人民出版社, 2012\",\n      \"field\": \"小 headword; PDF p. 76, printed p. 64; scanned headword and continuation checked on PDF p. 77, printed p. 65\",\n      \"text\": \"The scanned entry identifies 小 as pictographic and interprets its marks as tiny grains of dust or sand, calling it an early graph of 沙; it says the graph was extended to mean ‘small,’ opposite 大, and gives that sense in oracle-bone and bronze inscriptions. It cites 《粹》1004 for 小雨, then describes extensions to low status, contempt, and youth. It says the current form was corrupted in bronze inscriptions and treats Shuowen’s 八-plus-丨 account as an explanation of that altered form. The adjacent 少 entry says 小 and 少 were originally one graph, with similar use in oracle-bone texts, and later differentiated; its explanation continues onto printed p. 65. Direct scan inspection confirms the cited headword and passage. Forms checked against pixels: 小, 少, 沙, 八, 丨, 大, and the text’s citation 《粹》1004. The scan supports what this author asserts; it does not settle the disputed sand-grain interpretation.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"directly_inspected_book_scan\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.worldcat.org/search?q=9787552800692\",\n      \"title\": \"《字源》 (2012), PDF pp. 76–77; printed pp. 64–65\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-803fd94611bb57f92df9\",\n      \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n      \"field\": \"小: formation, early use and adjacent 少 entry\",\n      \"text\": \"The database reports two analyses of 小’s early marks: abstract dots for smallness, attributed to 商承祚 and 于省吾, or an early graph of 沙 depicting fine grains, attributed to 馬敘倫. It also describes 小 and 少 as an originally shared graph. Its examples include oracle-bone 小雨, time expressions 小食 and 小采, and bronze 小鼎, 小子 and 小臣. The page provides no absolute dates for these cited artifacts or usages, so it cannot alone establish a chronology among the senses.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_and_historical_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n      \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-5385acd88b51f476d32e\",\n      \"source\": \"金真姬,《常用漢字二百字探源》\",\n      \"field\": \"小, 字形探源／字義探源, PDF pp. 20–21; printed pp. 26–27\",\n      \"text\": \"The inspected entry reports disagreement about what the three dots represent, including raindrops, scattered objects or fine smallness. It favors an abstract indication of smallness and says later lengthened dots prompted Shuowen’s 八-plus-丨 analysis, which it rejects as based on the altered form. It cites oracle-bone 小雨, 小風 and 小牢 as uses for ‘small.’ This supports a competing scholarly account, not a settled referent for the dots.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"scholarly_reference\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.yjcn.nl/wp/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/%E5%B8%B8%E7用漢字二百字探源%EF%BC%88金真姬%EF%BC%89.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"《常用漢字二百字探源》, PDF pp. 20–21\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-5ac63eb9bb056d4dc7cb\",\n      \"source\": \"中央研究院, Academia Sinica Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"少 字形演變\",\n      \"text\": \"The page states that 少 and 小 were originally one graph depicting fine sand grains, with ‘small’ as the original meaning; it says the lower dot of 少 became a diagonal stroke in bronze inscriptions, distinguishing it from 小. This is an explicit shared-origin analysis, while other consulted sources retain competing analyses of 小’s dots.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"少\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10271\",\n      \"title\": \"漢字「少」：字形演變\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-b8ded469510aa9455741\",\n      \"source\": \"李學勤主編,《字源》\",\n      \"field\": \"小 headword; PDF p. 76, printed p. 64; continuation PDF p. 77, printed p. 65\",\n      \"text\": \"The inspected entry calls 小 pictographic, interpreting its marks as tiny dust or sand particles and describing 小 as an early graph of 沙. It says the graph extended to mean ‘small,’ opposite 大, and reports that sense in oracle-bone and bronze inscriptions, citing 《粹》1004 for 小雨. It describes later extensions to low status, contempt and youth. It says the graph had become corrupted in bronze inscriptions and treats Shuowen’s 八-plus-丨 account as an explanation of that altered form. The adjacent 少 entry says 小 and 少 were originally one graph, used similarly in oracle-bone texts, and later differentiated; its account continues on printed p. 65. Both attached page images were inspected. Forms checked against scan pixels: 小, 少, 沙, 八, 丨, 大, and 《粹》1004. This verifies what this author claims, not the disputed sand-grain interpretation.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"directly_inspected_book_scan\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.worldcat.org/search?q=9787552800692\",\n      \"title\": \"《字源》, 李學勤主編, 天津古籍出版社／遼寧人民出版社, 2012, PDF pp. 76–77; printed pp. 64–65\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-cfcd778e20a67d7860ec\",\n      \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n      \"field\": \"小 formation, early uses and adjacent 少, 沙 and 雀 records\",\n      \"text\": \"The database reports competing interpretations of 小’s early marks: abstract dots for smallness, attributed to 商承祚 and 于省吾, or an early graph of 沙 depicting fine grains, attributed to 馬敍倫. It says 小 and 少 were one graph before differentiation, and that oracle-bone forms could use four dots for 小/少. It reports 小雨, 小食 (afternoon), 小采 (dusk), and bronze 小鼎, 小子 and 小臣, without absolute dates for the cited artifacts or semantic developments. Its 沙 entry discusses several analyses of 沙 forms; thus the page does not establish that 沙 was borrowed phonetically from 小. Its 雀 entry says 小 contributes both ‘small bird’ and sound, while separately reporting varied early uses and graphic forms.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小; 少; 沙; 雀\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_and_historical_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n      \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-4029d7e014bdb7910f42\",\n      \"source\": \"中央研究院, Academia Sinica Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"小 字形演變\",\n      \"text\": \"The page labels oracle-bone, bronze, small-seal and Shuowen forms. It interprets the earlier marks as tiny sand grains scattered around, expressing smallness, and says the middle dot in small-seal script became a vertical stroke separating the two side marks. This is one source’s interpretation, not independent proof of the depicted referent.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n      \"title\": \"漢字「小」：字形演變\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-fe9ea9767e1da9fa626c\",\n      \"source\": \"教育部《異體字字典》, Taiwan Ministry of Education\",\n      \"field\": \"說文釋形; 釋義\",\n      \"text\": \"The dictionary preserves Xu Shen’s historical account: 小 means ‘the subtle/small among things’ and is analyzed as 八 and 丨, ‘seen and divided.’ It lists modern senses including small, make smaller, brief, young, lower-ranked, humble self-reference, slight degree and despise, with citations, but does not establish a chronological order among them.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?educode=A01068&powerMode=2\",\n      \"title\": \"教育部《異體字字典》：小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-9cae30a34adfac4e5d42\",\n      \"source\": \"Nohara, “The reconstruction of the word shao (少) in Old Chinese Phonology”\",\n      \"field\": \"少 and 小 sound relationship; discussion and reconstruction comparison, pp. 2–6, 16\",\n      \"text\": \"The inspected study summarizes two positions on the proposed sound relationship around 少: Zhengzhang and Pan allow relationships among 少, 小 and related forms through reconstructed nasal initials; Schuessler and Baxter–Sagart reject a 少–小 phonetic-series relationship, with Schuessler treating 小 as semantic rather than phonetic in the cited discussion. The study also documents that early spellings 少 and 小 can both represent the words ‘small’ and ‘few’ in some oracle-bone, bronze and Warring States materials, with orthographic practice differing across regions and periods. This supports caution about inferring a phonetic relation from shared early spelling or present form alone.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"少; 小\",\n      \"kind\": \"scholarly_study\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/339973841_The_reconstruction_of_the_word_shao_shao_in_Old_Chinese_Phonology_shaonoshangguyinnitsuite\",\n      \"title\": \"「少」の上古音について／The reconstruction of the word shao (少) in Old Chinese Phonology\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-142dfc94245bc8e052bc\",\n      \"source\": \"Baxter and Sagart, Old Chinese reconstruction version 1.1\",\n      \"field\": \"Search result for author-hosted reconstruction table; PDF could not be opened in this invocation\",\n      \"text\": \"Search surfaced the authors’ version 1.1 table PDF, but the browser failed to open it. No specific 小, 少, 沙 or 雀 row was independently inspected in this invocation, so no table readings are asserted here.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小; 少; 沙; 雀\",\n      \"kind\": \"access_failure\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ocbaxtersagart.lsait.lsa.umich.edu/BaxterSagartOCbyMandarinMC2014-09-20.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"Baxter-Sagart Old Chinese reconstruction, version 1.1\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-46ffd93eb016aa392f31\",\n      \"source\": \"李學勤主編,《字源》, 天津古籍出版社／遼寧人民出版社, 2012, ISBN 9787552800692\",\n      \"field\": \"小 headword; PDF p. 76, printed p. 64\",\n      \"text\": \"The entry calls 小 pictographic and interprets its marks as tiny dust or sand particles, an early graph of 沙. It says the graph was extended to mean ‘small,’ opposite 大, and cites oracle-bone and bronze uses, including 《粹》1004 小雨. It also describes extensions to low status, contempt and youth, and says the bronze form had become corrupted, prompting Shuowen’s 八-plus-丨 explanation. Both attached page images were inspected; the printed headword, cited forms 小, 沙, 大, 八, 丨 and 《粹》1004 are legible. This verifies the author’s account, not the disputed sand interpretation.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"directly_inspected_book_scan\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.worldcat.org/search?q=9787552800692\",\n      \"title\": \"《字源》, 李學勤主編, 2012, PDF p. 76; printed p. 64\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-c673b3b25eff702eb8d9\",\n      \"source\": \"李學勤主編,《字源》, 天津古籍出版社／遼寧人民出版社, 2012, ISBN 9787552800692\",\n      \"field\": \"Adjacent 少 entry; PDF p. 76 and continuation p. 77, printed pp. 64–65\",\n      \"text\": \"The adjacent 少 entry says 小 and 少 were originally one graph and were used alike in oracle-bone texts, then differentiated; it describes 少’s final diagonal stroke as a distinguishing mark. The entry continues onto printed p. 65. Both source scans were inspected; the relevant 少 and 小 forms are legible. This is the book author’s graphic account, not proof of a historical sound relationship.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"少; 小\",\n      \"kind\": \"directly_inspected_book_scan\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.worldcat.org/search?q=9787552800692\",\n      \"title\": \"《字源》, 李學勤主編, 2012, PDF pp. 76–77; printed pp. 64–65\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-047697228b315d31e79e\",\n      \"source\": \"漢語多功能字庫, Chinese University of Hong Kong\",\n      \"field\": \"小, 少 and 沙 records: formation, cited uses and graph components\",\n      \"text\": \"The 小 record presents two analyses of its early marks: abstract dots for smallness, attributed to 商承祚 and 于省吾, or an early graph of 沙 depicting fine sand grains, attributed to 馬敍倫. It reports 小雨, 小食 as an afternoon expression, 小采 as a dusk expression, and bronze uses including 小鼎, 小子 and 小臣, without absolute artifact dates. Its 少 record says early forms could overlap and that three-dot and four-dot spellings later distinguished 小 and 少. The 沙 account reports competing analyses of bronze uses, so the cited pages do not establish a phonetic borrowing of 沙 from 小.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小; 少; 沙\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_and_historical_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n      \"title\": \"漢語多功能字庫：漢字甲骨部件分析—小\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-0ec345d60e9fc6dc0872\",\n      \"source\": \"中央研究院, Academia Sinica Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"少 字形演變\",\n      \"text\": \"The database asserts that 少 and 小 were originally one graph depicting fine sand grains, with ‘small’ as the original meaning, and says the lowest dot of 少 became a diagonal stroke in bronze inscriptions. This supports that interpretation as a source-attributed account; CUHK presents competing analyses of 小’s marks.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"少\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10271\",\n      \"title\": \"漢字「少」：字形演變\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-1fc728b859bc4669b67d\",\n      \"source\": \"中央研究院, Academia Sinica Character Database\",\n      \"field\": \"小 字形演變\",\n      \"text\": \"The page labels oracle-bone, bronze, small-seal and Shuowen forms. It interprets the earlier marks as scattered fine sand grains expressing smallness and says the middle dot became a vertical stroke separating the two side marks in small-seal script. This is the database’s interpretation, not independent proof of the marks’ referent.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"小\",\n      \"kind\": \"paleographic_dictionary\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n      \"title\": \"漢字「小」：字形演變\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"X-1b31b87c8aa5370dbe65\",\n      \"source\": \"Masaki Nohara, “The reconstruction of the word shao (少) in Old Chinese Phonology,” 中国語学 262 (2015), pp. 57–75\",\n      \"field\": \"少–小 phonetic relationship and early orthographic usage, especially PDF pp. 59–65\",\n      \"text\": \"Nohara reviews competing Old Chinese analyses. Zhengzhang and Pan allow links among 少, 小 and related forms via proposed nasal initials, while Schuessler and Baxter–Sagart reject a 少–小 phonetic-series relation in the discussion Nohara cites. Nohara argues that excavated-text spelling and sound evidence do not warrant treating the early graphic overlap as proof of a phonetic relationship. The paper also documents that 少 and 小 spellings could represent both ‘few’ and ‘small’ in some early materials, with regional and period differences.\",\n      \"record_character\": \"少; 小\",\n      \"kind\": \"scholarly_study\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/chuugokugogaku/2015/262/2015_57/_pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"「少」の上古音について／The reconstruction of the word shao (少) in Old Chinese Phonology\",\n      \"accessed_at\": \"2026-10-02\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"context\": {\n    \"provenance\": \"Base evidence consists of imported local JSONL excerpts. Source names identify upstream datasets; extraction may lose sense and language boundaries. Further external evidence and research activity are documented separately in the dossier.\",\n    \"editorial_rules\": [\n      \"Write about the character's graphic history; distinguish it from the history of a spoken word.\",\n      \"Separate historical explanation from mnemonics. Do not infer history from modern shapes or readings.\",\n      \"Sources may repeat one another. A source count is not independent corroboration.\",\n      \"Treat Shuowen as a historical account, not automatic confirmation. Its generated English glosses are excluded.\",\n      \"Unrelated word senses may appear in Wiktionary excerpts. Do not merge them into a character origin.\",\n      \"Related-character evidence retains its record_character. Do not silently transfer a traditional form's components to a simplified form.\",\n      \"No glyph image has been visually inspected in this packet. Do not claim to have inspected one.\",\n      \"Explain missing evidence explicitly, especially for Japanese-created characters. A Chinese spelling pronunciation is not evidence for a Japanese origin.\"\n    ],\n    \"unverified_pipeline_metadata\": {\n      \"formation_type\": \"ideographic\",\n      \"formation_type_conflict\": {\n        \"makemeahanzi\": \"ideographic\",\n        \"dong_chinese\": \"other\",\n        \"shuowen_jiezi\": \"ideographic\",\n        \"wiktionary\": \"pictographic\"\n      },\n      \"formation_details\": null,\n      \"variants\": null\n    }\n  },\n  \"external_research\": {\n    \"search_audit\": [\n      {\n        \"query\": \"小 character oracle bone bronze inscriptions etymology Shuowen paleography; 小 說文 甲骨文 金文 字形 演變 小 字源; site:zi.tools 小 paleography bronze oracle bone 小; 小 少 relation Old Chinese Schuessler 2007\",\n        \"urls\": [\n          \"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=10269\",\n          \"https://scholarworks.iu.edu/dspace/items/b5a7377f-6b01-4704-a136-6b40a4d04078\",\n          \"https://www.guoxuedashi.com/zixing/yanbian/3081ht/\",\n          \"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%E5%B0%8F\"\n        ],\n        \"outcome\": \"Opened Academia Sinica’s 小 evolution page and Wiktionary entry. Guoxuedashi result was later blocked by a verification page. Search results surfaced but did not establish the cited secondary Schuessler analysis.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"query\": \"site:unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5C0F 小 kMandarin; site:ocbaxtersagart.lsait.lsa.umich.edu 小 沙 Old Chinese Baxter Sagart 2014; 小 最早 用例 甲骨文 小 大 說文 字義 殷周\",\n        \"urls\": [\n          \"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/oraclePiece.php?piece=%E5%B0%8F&sub=1\",\n          \"https://xiaoxue.iis.sinica.edu.tw/jiaguwen\",\n          \"https://www.zdic.net/hans/%E5%B0%8F\",\n          \"https://ctext.org/dictionary.pl?if=gb&rad=42\",\n          \"https://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?educode=A01068&powerMode=2\",\n          \"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=%E5%B0%8F\"\n        ],\n        \"outcome\": \"Opened CUHK, Taiwan Ministry of Education and Academia Sinica pages. The requested Unihan endpoint returned an internal fetch error. CUHK provided early usage examples and competing graphic analyses.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"query\": \"site:unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5C0F; Unihan 小 U+5C0F kMandarin xiǎo Unicode; \\\"小雨\\\" \\\"《粹》1004\\\" 甲骨\",\n        \"urls\": [\n          \"https://unicode.org/faq/han_cjk.html\",\n          \"https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr38/tr38-3.html\",\n          \"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%E5%B0%8F\",\n          \"https://www.unicode.org/charts/unihan.html\",\n          \"https://www.yjcn.nl/wp/wp-content/uploads/2015/11/%E5%B8%B8%E7%94%A8%E6%BC%A2%E5%AD%97%E4%BA%8C%E7%99%BE%E5%AD%9